osition marking static location or target. 환경에 안전하다 = ''safe to/for the environment''.", "example_in_sentence": "환경에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다는 것이에요", "exp": "Explains a point: ''it is (the fact) that…''. 안전하다 → 안전하다는 것이에요 (is that it is safe).", "example_in_sentence": "안전하다는 것이에요"}]}, {"text": "다 쓴 후에는 그냥 자연에 버려도 괜찮아요.", "translation": "After it''s used up, you can simply dispose of it in nature without worry.", "vocab": [{"ko": "쓰다", "en": "to use; to write", "note": ""}, {"ko": "후", "en": "after; afterwards", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자연", "en": "nature", "note": ""}, {"ko": "버리다", "en": "to throw away; to discard", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 후에", "exp": "Means ''after doing''. 쓰다 → 쓴 후에 (after using). 다 쓴 후에는 = after it is all used up.", "example_in_sentence": "다 쓴 후에는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (location/time)", "exp": "Static location postposition. 자연에 = ''in/to nature''.", "example_in_sentence": "자연에"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~아/어도 괜찮다", "exp": "Gives permission: ''it''s okay to…''. 버리다 → 버려도 괜찮아요 (it''s fine to throw it away).", "example_in_sentence": "버려도 괜찮아요"}]}, {"text": "일반 배터리와 달리 환경을 오염시키지 않아요.", "translation": "Unlike regular batteries, it does not pollute the environment.", "vocab": [{"ko": "일반", "en": "general; ordinary; regular", "note": ""}, {"ko": "배터리", "en": "battery", "note": ""}, {"ko": "환경", "en": "environment", "note": ""}, {"ko": "오염시키다", "en": "to pollute; to contaminate", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "Direct object particle. 환경을 = ''environment (direct object)''.", "example_in_sentence": "환경을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않다", "exp": "Long form of ''not''. 오염시키다 → 오염시키지 않아요 (does not pollute).", "example_in_sentence": "오염시키지 않아요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~와 달리 (unlike; in contrast to)", "exp": "Fixed postpositional phrase marking contrast. 일반 배터리와 달리 = ''unlike regular batteries / in contrast to regular batteries''.", "example_in_sentence": "일반 배터리와 달리"}]}, {"text": "한국에서도 배터리 문제는 중요해요.", "translation": "Battery issues are important in Korea too.", "vocab": [{"ko": "한국", "en": "Korea", "note": ""}, {"ko": "배터리", "en": "battery", "note": ""}, {"ko": "문제", "en": "problem; issue", "note": ""}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서도", "exp": "에서 (in) + 도 (also) = also in. 한국에서도 = in Korea too.", "example_in_sentence": "한국에서도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle. 문제는 = ''as for the issue / the issue (is)''.", "example_in_sentence": "문제는"}]}, {"text": "스마트폰이나 전기차에 들어가는 배터리를 어떻게 처리할지 고민이 많거든요.", "translation": "There are many concerns about how to handle batteries used in smartphones and electric vehicles.", "vocab": [{"ko": "스마트폰", "en": "smartphone", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전기차", "en": "electric vehicle", "note": ""}, {"ko": "배터리", "en": "battery", "note": ""}, {"ko": "처리하다", "en": "to handle; to process; to dispose of", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)나 (or / about / as much as)", "exp": "Alternation, approximation particle. 스마트폰이나 = ''smartphone or (and)''. Lists alternatives.", "example_in_sentence": "스마트폰이나"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (location/time)", "exp": "Locative postposition. 전기차에 들어가다 = ''enter/go into electric vehicles = used in EVs''.", "example_in_sentence": "전기차에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/는 (present tense attributive modifier)", "exp": "Present attributive suffix modifying noun. 들어가다 → 들어가는 = ''entering/used (modifying batteries)''.", "example_in_sentence": "들어가는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "Direct object particle. 배터리를 = ''batteries (direct object)''.", "example_in_sentence": "배터리를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ지", "exp": "Puts a question inside a sentence: ''how to…''. 처리하다 → 어떻게 처리할지 (how to deal with it).", "example_in_sentence": "어떻게 처리할지"}, {"type": "grammar", "