지 (until)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Postposition marking limit or boundary in time/sequence. 24세기까지 = ''until/up to the 24th century''.", "ex_ko": "이 배터리는 24세기까지 사용할 수 있다고 해요.", "ex_en": "They say this battery can be used until the 24th century."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''can''. 사용하다 → 사용할 수 있다 (can be used).", "ex_ko": "이 배터리는 24세기까지 사용할 수 있다고 해요.", "ex_en": "They say this battery can be used until the 24th century."}, {"name": "~다고 하다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Reports what others say: ''they say that…''. 사용할 수 있다 → 사용할 수 있다고 해요.", "ex_ko": "이 배터리는 24세기까지 사용할 수 있다고 해요.", "ex_en": "They say this battery can be used until the 24th century."}, {"name": "~부터 (from)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Postposition marking starting point in time or sequence. 지금부터 = ''from now; starting now''.", "ex_ko": "지금부터 약 800년 동안 쓸 수 있다는 뜻이에요.", "ex_en": "It means it can be used for approximately 800 years from now."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다/없다 (ability/possibility)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Expresses ability/possibility. 보다 → 볼 수 있다 = ''can see / be able to see''.", "ex_ko": "지금부터 약 800년 동안 쓸 수 있다는 뜻이에요.", "ex_en": "It means it can be used for approximately 800 years from now."}, {"name": "~다는 뜻이에요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''it means that…''. 쓸 수 있다 → 쓸 수 있다는 뜻이에요.", "ex_ko": "지금부터 약 800년 동안 쓸 수 있다는 뜻이에요.", "ex_en": "It means it can be used for approximately 800 years from now."}, {"name": "~의 (possessive)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Possessive/attributive particle. 배터리의 점 = ''point/feature of the battery''.", "ex_ko": "이 배터리의 가장 좋은 점은 환경에 안전하다는 것이에요.", "ex_en": "The best feature of this battery is that it is safe for the environment."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/은 (past verb / present adj modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Attributive suffix for adjective or past verb modifying noun. 좋다 → 좋은 = ''good (modifying point)''.", "ex_ko": "이 배터리의 가장 좋은 점은 환경에 안전하다는 것이에요.", "ex_en": "The best feature of this battery is that it is safe for the environment."}, {"name": "~에 (location/time)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Postposition marking static location or target. 환경에 안전하다 = ''safe to/for the environment''.", "ex_ko": "이 배터리의 가장 좋은 점은 환경에 안전하다는 것이에요.", "ex_en": "The best feature of this battery is that it is safe for the environment."}, {"name": "~다는 것이에요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Explains a point: ''it is (the fact) that…''. 안전하다 → 안전하다는 것이에요 (is that it is safe).", "ex_ko": "이 배터리의 가장 좋은 점은 환경에 안전하다는 것이에요.", "ex_en": "The best feature of this battery is that it is safe for the environment."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ 후에", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''after doing''. 쓰다 → 쓴 후에 (after using). 다 쓴 후에는 = after it is all used up.", "ex_ko": "다 쓴 후에는 그냥 자연에 버려도 괜찮아요.", "ex_en": "After it''s used up, you can simply dispose of it in nature without worry."}, {"name": "~을/를 (object marker)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Direct object particle. 환경을 = ''environment (direct object)''.", "ex_ko": "일반 배터리와 달리 환경을 오염시키지 않아요.", "ex_en": "Unlike regular batteries, it does not pollute the environment."}, {"name": "~지 않다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Long form of ''not''. 오염시키다 → 오염시키지 않아요 (does not pollute).", "ex_ko": "일반 배터리와 달리 환경을 오염시키지 않아요.", "ex_en": "Unlike regular batteries, it does not pollute the environment."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mowq59qac7z9' and md5(translation) = 'bb7f7b9c99926306acc2d96d69b18331';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Two people paddleboarding in Australia rescued a special animal. They discovered a wallaby struggling in the ocean. A wallaby is an Australian animal similar to a kangaroo. It normally lives on land, but this wallaby drifted out to sea. It couldn''t return to shore on its own. The two people immediately helped the wallaby. They got close on their paddleboard and brought it to a safe place. The wallaby was rescued safely. This story touched many people on the internet. The love for animals gave hope to people all around the world.", "Korea''s teacher shortage becomes serious, causing disruption to school classes", "What is an \"anxiety bag\"? A popular trend", "The US and China resume talks over trade issues", "\"Talking pig\" becomes a social media star", "The \"nothing maxing\" trend of doing nothing spreads"], "sentences": [{"text": "호주에서 패들보드를 타던 두 사람이 특별한 동물을 구조했어요.", "translation": "Two people who were riding a paddleboard in Australia rescued a special animal.", "vocab": [{"ko": "호주", "en": "Australia"}, {"ko": "패들보드", "en": "paddleboard"}, {"ko": "구조하다", "en": "to rescue"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~던", "exp": "Describes something that was going on in the past. 타다 → 타던 사람 (people who were riding).", "example_in_sentence": "패들보드를 타던"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 구조하다 → 구조했어요 (rescued).", "example_in_sentence": "구조했어요"}]}, {"text": "바다에서 힘들어하는 왈라비 한 마리를 발견했어요.", "translation": "They discovered one wallaby struggling in the sea.", "vocab": [{"ko": "바다", "en": "sea"}, {"ko": "힘들어하다", "en": "to struggle; to have difficulty"}, {"ko": "왈라비", "en": "wallaby"}, {"ko": "발견하다", "en": "to discover"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는", "exp": "Present attributive form. Describes an action happening at the moment of discovery. 힘들어하다 + ~는 = ''struggling''.", "example_in_sentence": "힘들어하는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "number + 마리", "exp": "마리 is the counter for animals. 왈라비 한 마리 = one wallaby.", "example_in_sentence": "한 마리"}]}, {"text": "왈라비는 캥거루와 비슷한 호주 동물이에요.", "translation": "The wallaby is an Australian animal similar to a kangaroo.", "vocab": [{"ko": "캥거루", "en": "kangaroo"}, {"ko": "비슷하다", "en": "to be similar"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Adjective form used before a noun. 비슷하다 → 비슷한 (similar).", "example_in_sentence": "비슷한"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이에요", "exp": "Present copula for polite speech. Links subject to predicate noun. Used when preceding noun ends in consonant.", "example_in_sentence": "이에요"}]}, {"text": "보통 땅에서 살지만 이 왈라비는 바다로 떠내려갔어요.", "translation": "Usually they live on land, but this wallaby drifted out to sea.", "vocab": [{"ko": "보통", "en": "usually"}, {"ko": "떠내려가다", "en": "to drift away; to be carried away"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지만", "exp": "Conjunctive ending expressing contrast. Connects two clauses with opposing meanings. 살다 + ~지만 = ''live but''.", "example_in_sentence": "살지만"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 떠내려가다 → 떠내려갔어요 (drifted away).", "example_in_sentence": "떠내려갔어요"}]}, {"text": "혼자서는 육지로 돌아갈 수 없었어요.", "translation": "It could not return to land by itself.", "vocab": [{"ko": "혼자", "en": "alone; by oneself"}, {"ko": "육지", "en": "land"}, {"ko": "돌아가다", "en": "to return"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 없다", "exp": "Means ''cannot''. 돌아가다 → 돌아갈 수 없었어요 (could not go back).", "example_in_sentence": "돌아갈 수 없었어요"}]}, {"text": "두 사람은 바로 왈라비를 도와주었어요.", "translation": "The two people immediately helped the wallaby.", "vocab": [{"ko": "바로", "en": "immediately; right away"}, {"ko": "도와주다", "en": "to help"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 주다", "exp": "Shows doing something for someone. 돕다 → 도와 + 주다 = 도와주다 (to help someone).", "example_in_sentence": "도와주었어요"}]}, {"text": "패들보드로 가까이 가서 안전한 곳으로 데려갔어요.", "translation": "They went close by paddleboard and took it to a safe place.", "vocab": [{"ko": "가까이", "en": "close; near"}, {"ko": "안전하다", "en": "to be safe"}, {"ko": "데려가다", "en": "to take (someone) along"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어서", "exp": "Links actions in order: ''and then''. 가다 → 가서 (went, and then…).", "example_in_sentence": "가까이 가서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Adjective form used before a noun. 안전하다 → 안전한 곳 (a safe place).", "example_in_sentence": "안전한 곳"}]}, {"text": "왈라비는 무사히 구조되었어요.", "translation": "The wallaby was safely rescued.", "vocab": [{"ko": "무사히", "en": "safely; without harm"}, {"ko": "구조되다", "en": "to be rescued"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 구조되다 → 구조되었어요 (was rescued).", "example_in_sentence": "구조되었어요"}]}, {"text": "이 이야기는 인터넷에서 많은 사람들에게 감동을 주었어요.", "translation": "This story touched many people on the internet.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이야기", "en": "story"}, {"ko": "인터넷", "en": "internet"}, {"ko": "감동", "en": "being moved; inspiration"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에게", "exp": "Dative particle marking indirect object (recipient). 사람들 + ~에게 = ''to people''. Shows who receives the action.", "example_in_sentence": "사람들에게"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "감동을 주다", "exp": "Idiom meaning ''to inspire; to move emotionally''. Transitive expression with abstract object.", "example_in_sentence": "감동을 주었어요"}]}, {"text": "동물을 사랑하는 마음이 전 세계 사람들에게 희망을 주었어요.", "translation": "Their love for animals gave hope to people all over the world.", "vocab": [{"ko": "동물", "en": "animal"}, {"ko": "사랑하다", "en": "to love"}, {"ko": "마음", "en": "heart; mind"}, {"ko": "희망", "en": "hope"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는", "exp": "Present attributive form. 사랑하다 + ~는 = ''loving''. Modifies the noun 마음 (heart).", "example_in_sentence": "사랑하는"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "희망을 주다", "exp": "Idiom meaning ''to give hope''. Abstract object 희망 with the verb 주다 (to give).", "example_in_sentence": "희망을 주었어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "호주", "en": "Australia", "note": ""}, {"ko": "패들보드", "en": "paddleboard", "note": ""}, {"ko": "구조하다", "en": "to rescue", "note": ""}, {"ko": "바다", "en": "sea", "note": ""}, {"ko": "힘들어하다", "en": "to struggle; to have difficulty", "note": ""}, {"ko": "왈라비", "en": "wallaby", "note": ""}, {"ko": "발견하다", "en": "to discover", "note": ""}, {"ko": "캥거루", "en": "kangaroo", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비슷하다", "en": "to be similar", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보통", "en": "usually", "note": ""}, {"ko": "떠내려가다", "en": "to drift away; to be carried away", "note": ""}, {"ko": "혼자", "en": "alone; by oneself", "note": ""}, {"ko": "육지", "en": "land", "note": ""}, {"ko": "돌아가다", "en": "to return", "note": ""}, {"ko": "바로", "en": "immediately; right away", "note": ""}, {"ko": "도와주다", "en": "to help", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가까이", "en": "close; near", "note": ""}, {"ko": "안전하다", "en": "to be safe", "note": ""}, {"ko": "데려가다", "en": "to take (someone) along", "note": ""}, {"ko": "무사히", "en": "safely; without harm", "note": ""}, {"ko": "구조되다", "en": "to be rescued", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이야기", "en": "story", "note": ""}, {"ko": "인터넷", "en": "internet", "note": ""}, {"ko": "감동", "en": "being moved; inspiration", "note": ""}, {"ko": "동물", "en": "animal", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사랑하다", "en": "to love", "note": ""}, {"ko": "마음", "en": "heart; mind", "note": ""}, {"ko": "희망", "en": "hope", "note": ""}, {"ko": "패들보드를 타다", "en": "to paddleboard; to ride a paddleboard", "note": "타다 = to ride/board. 패들보드 is the paddleboard itself."}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special; special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "살다", "en": "to live; to inhabit; to dwell", "note": ""}, {"ko": "혼자서", "en": "alone; by oneself; on its own", "note": "혼자 = alone; 서 emphasizes independent action."}, {"ko": "안전한", "en": "safe; secure", "note": ""}, {"ko": "감동을 주다", "en": "to move (emotionally); to touch; to inspire", "note": "감동 = emotional impact/inspiration; 주다 = to give."}, {"ko": "전 세계", "en": "the whole world; worldwide; all over the world", "note": "전 = whole/entire; 세계 = world."}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~던", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Describes something that was going on in the past. 타다 → 타던 사람 (people who were riding).", "ex_ko": "호주에서 패들보드를 타던 두 사람이 특별한 동물을 구조했어요.", "ex_en": "Two people who were riding a paddleboard in Australia rescued a special animal."}, {"name": "~았/었어요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 떠내려가다 → 떠내려갔어요 (drifted away).", "ex_ko": "호주에서 패들보드를 타던 두 사람이 특별한 동물을 구조했어요.", "ex_en": "Two people who were riding a paddleboard in Australia rescued a special animal."}, {"name": "~는", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Present attributive form. Describes an action happening at the moment of discovery. 힘들어하다 + ~는 = ''struggling''.", "ex_ko": "바다에서 힘들어하는 왈라비 한 마리를 발견했어요.", "ex_en": "They discovered one wallaby struggling in the sea."}, {"name": "number + 마리", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "마리 is the counter for animals. 왈라비 한 마리 = one wallaby.", "ex_ko": "바다에서 힘들어하는 왈라비 한 마리를 발견했어요.", "ex_en": "They discovered one wallaby struggling in the sea."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Adjective form used before a noun. 안전하다 → 안전한 곳 (a safe place).", "ex_ko": "왈라비는 캥거루와 비슷한 호주 동물이에요.", "ex_en": "The wallaby is an Australian animal similar to a kangaroo."}, {"name": "~이에요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Present copula for polite speech. Links subject to predicate noun. Used when preceding noun ends in consonant.", "ex_ko": "왈라비는 캥거루와 비슷한 호주 동물이에요.", "ex_en": "The wallaby is an Australian animal similar to a kangaroo."}, {"name": "~지만", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Conjunctive ending expressing contrast. Connects two clauses with opposing meanings. 살다 + ~지만 = ''live but''.", "ex_ko": "보통 땅에서 살지만 이 왈라비는 바다로 떠내려갔어요.", "ex_en": "Usually they live on land, but this wallaby drifted out to sea."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 없다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''cannot''. 돌아가다 → 돌아갈 수 없었어요 (could not go back).", "ex_ko": "혼자서는 육지로 돌아갈 수 없었어요.", "ex_en": "It could not return to land by itself."}, {"name": "~아/어 주다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Shows doing something for someone. 돕다 → 도와 + 주다 = 도와주다 (to help someone).", "ex_ko": "두 사람은 바로 왈라비를 도와주었어요.", "ex_en": "The two people immediately helped the wallaby."}, {"name": "~아/어서", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Links actions in order: ''and then''. 가다 → 가서 (went, and then…).", "ex_ko": "패들보드로 가까이 가서 안전한 곳으로 데려갔어요.", "ex_en": "They went close by paddleboard and took it to a safe place."}, {"name": "~에게", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Dative particle marking indirect object (recipient). 사람들 + ~에게 = ''to people''. Shows who receives the action.", "ex_ko": "이 이야기는 인터넷에서 많은 사람들에게 감동을 주었어요.", "ex_en": "This story touched many people on the internet."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moxoqjdmdrtw' and md5(translation) = '174ee0e822212d824557df4330fa0d3c';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"sentences": [{"text": "1958년 한 장의 사진이 화제가 되고 있어요.", "idx": 0, "translation": "A photograph from 1958 is becoming a topic of conversation.", "vocab": [{"ko": "화제", "en": "topic, issue", "note": "commonly used for news or trending subjects"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~이 되다", "exp": "something becomes or turns into a state", "example_in_sentence": "화제가 되고"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "당시 32세였던 데이비드 아텐버러와 10세 찰스 왕세자가 함께 찍은 사진입니다.", "idx": 1, "translation": "It is a photo of David Attenborough, then 32, and 10-year-old Prince Charles taken together.", "vocab": [{"ko": "당시", "en": "at that time, then", "note": "formal/written style for ''that time''"}, {"ko": "왕세자", "en": "crown prince", "note": "specific title for heir to throne"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~던", "exp": "past state or action that was ongoing; used in modifying clauses", "example_in_sentence": "당시 32세였던"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "데이비드 아텐버러는 영국의 유명한 자연 다큐멘터리 제작자예요.", "idx": 2, "translation": "David Attenborough is a famous British nature documentary maker.", "vocab": [{"ko": "자연", "en": "nature", "note": "as in ''nature documentary''"}, {"ko": "다큐멘터리", "en": "documentary", "note": "foreign loanword"}, {"ko": "제작자", "en": "producer, maker", "note": "agent noun from 제작(make)"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "지금은 90대 할아버지가 되었지만 여전히 활발하게 활동하고 있습니다.", "idx": 3, "translation": "Although he is now a grandfather in his 90s, he still continues to work actively.", "vocab": [{"ko": "활발하다", "en": "to be active; lively", "note": "adjective describing manner of activity"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~지만", "exp": "but, although; indicates contrast between two clauses", "example_in_sentence": "할아버지가 되었지만 여전히"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "찰스는 현재 영국의 왕이 되었어요.", "idx": 4, "translation": "Charles has now become the king of Britain.", "vocab": [], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~게 되다", "exp": "to come to be, to become (a change of state)", "example_in_sentence": "왕이 되었어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "68년 전 사진 속 두 사람은 모두 어려 보여요.", "idx": 5, "translation": "In the photograph from 68 years ago, both people appear young.", "vocab": [{"ko": "어려 보이다", "en": "to look young, appear young", "note": "어리다 + 보이다 construction"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "아텐버러는 지금처럼 하얀 머리가 아니었고, 찰스는 아직 어린 왕자였습니다.", "idx": 6, "translation": "Attenborough did not have white hair as he does now, and Charles was still a young prince.", "vocab": [{"ko": "하얗다", "en": "to be white", "note": "descriptive form of 하얗다"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~지 않다", "exp": "negation; not doing/being something", "example_in_sentence": "머리가 아니었고"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 사진은 시간의 흐름을 보여주는 특별한 기록이에요.", "idx": 7, "translation": "This photograph is a special record showing the flow of time.", "vocab": [{"ko": "흐름", "en": "flow, passage", "note": "abstract noun from 흐르다"}, {"ko": "기록", "en": "record, recording", "note": "can mean physical or written record"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~는 것", "exp": "nominalizes a verb; ''the act/thing of doing''", "example_in_sentence": "흐름을 보여주는"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "두 사람 모두 각자 분야에서 중요한 역할을 하게 된 것이 흥미롭습니다.", "idx": 8, "translation": "It is interesting that both people have come to play important roles in their respective fields.", "vocab": [{"ko": "각자", "en": "respectively, each, individually", "note": "emphasizes separate/individual action"}, {"ko": "분야", "en": "field, domain", "note": "professional or subject area"}, {"ko": "역할", "en": "role, function", "note": "part played in a system"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~게 된 것이", "exp": "the fact that it came to be/happen; expressing how a state developed", "example_in_sentence": "하게 된 것이 흥미롭습니다"}], "analysis": []}], "version": "p2"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "화제", "en": "topic, issue", "note": "commonly used for news or trending subjects"}, {"ko": "당시", "en": "at that time, then", "note": "formal/written style for ''that time''"}, {"ko": "왕세자", "en": "crown prince", "note": "specific title for heir to throne"}, {"ko": "자연", "en": "nature", "note": "as in ''nature documentary''"}, {"ko": "다큐멘터리", "en": "documentary", "note": "foreign loanword"}, {"ko": "제작자", "en": "producer, maker", "note": "agent noun from 제작(make)"}, {"ko": "활발하다", "en": "to be active; lively", "note": "adjective describing manner of activity"}, {"ko": "어려 보이다", "en": "to look young, appear young", "note": "어리다 + 보이다 construction"}, {"ko": "하얗다", "en": "to be white", "note": "descriptive form of 하얗다"}, {"ko": "흐름", "en": "flow, passage", "note": "abstract noun from 흐르다"}, {"ko": "기록", "en": "record, recording", "note": "can mean physical or written record"}, {"ko": "각자", "en": "respectively, each, individually", "note": "emphasizes separate/individual action"}, {"ko": "분야", "en": "field, domain", "note": "professional or subject area"}, {"ko": "역할", "en": "role, function", "note": "part played in a system"}, {"ko": "화제가 되다", "en": "to become a hot topic; to become the subject of discussion", "note": "흔히 뉴스나 소셜 미디어에서 많은 사람들이 얘기하는 것을 의미함"}, {"ko": "함께", "en": "together; with each other", "note": "함께 + 동사로 ''같이 하다''의 의미"}, {"ko": "할아버지", "en": "grandfather; old person", "note": "여기서는 나이가 많은 사람을 뜻함"}, {"ko": "어리다", "en": "to be young; to look young", "note": "나이가 적거나 젊어 보이는 상태"}, {"ko": "흥미롭다", "en": "fascinating; interesting", "note": "흥미를 끌거나 재미있는 상태"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": []}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moxores2rrfe' and md5(translation) = '761e62506f84d3a766e56db4ec297cd2';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"sentences": [{"text": "1935년 미국에서 후버댐을 만들고 있었어요.", "idx": 0, "translation": "In 1935, they were building the Hoover Dam in the United States.", "vocab": [{"ko": "후버댐", "en": "Hoover Dam", "note": "proper noun; a famous dam in the USA"}, {"ko": "만들다", "en": "to build, to make", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~고 있었어요", "exp": "Past continuous: an action that was ongoing at a specific time in the past.", "example_in_sentence": "만들고 있었어요"}, {"pattern": "~에서", "exp": "Location marker indicating where an action takes place.", "example_in_sentence": "미국에서"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "댐은 물을 막아서 전기를 만드는 큰 건물이에요.", "idx": 1, "translation": "A dam is a large structure that holds back water to make electricity.", "vocab": [{"ko": "댐", "en": "dam", "note": ""}, {"ko": "물", "en": "water", "note": ""}, {"ko": "막다", "en": "to block, to stop", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전기", "en": "electricity", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~을/를 막아서", "exp": "Object marker with a connective showing purpose or method: blocking water in order to make electricity.", "example_in_sentence": "물을 막아서"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "공사 관계자들이 댐 안의 큰 파이프를 타고 있어요.", "idx": 2, "translation": "Construction workers are riding on a big pipe inside the dam.", "vocab": [{"ko": "공사 관계자", "en": "construction staff", "note": ""}, {"ko": "파이프", "en": "pipe", "note": ""}, {"ko": "타다", "en": "to ride; to get on", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~고 있어요", "exp": "Present continuous: an action happening now.", "example_in_sentence": "타고 있어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 파이프는 물이 지나가는 통로예요.", "idx": 3, "translation": "This pipe is a passage where water flows through.", "vocab": [{"ko": "통로", "en": "passage, channel, corridor", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지나가다", "en": "to pass through, to go by", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ/은 것", "exp": "Nominalizer: turning a clause into a noun phrase; ''(something) that water passes through''.", "example_in_sentence": "물이 지나가는 통로"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "펜스톡 파이프라고 불러요.", "idx": 4, "translation": "It is called a penstock pipe.", "vocab": [{"ko": "펜스톡", "en": "penstock", "note": "a type of pipe in a dam"}, {"ko": "부르다", "en": "to call, to name", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~라고 부르다", "exp": "To call/name something with a specific name or term.", "example_in_sentence": "펜스톡 파이프라고 불러요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "후버댐은 거의 완성되어 가고 있었어요.", "idx": 5, "translation": "The Hoover Dam was almost finished.", "vocab": [{"ko": "거의", "en": "almost, nearly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "완성되다", "en": "to be completed", "note": "passive/resultative form of 완성하다"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~어지고 있었어요", "exp": "Past continuous of a change or process: the dam was in the process of being completed.", "example_in_sentence": "완성되어 가고 있었어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 댐은 지금도 미국에서 중요한 전력을 만들고 있어요.", "idx": 6, "translation": "This dam still produces important electricity in the United States today.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지금", "en": "now", "note": ""}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전력", "en": "electric power, electricity", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~고 있어요", "exp": "Present continuous: an action or state ongoing now.", "example_in_sentence": "만들고 있어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "당시 사진을 보면 댐의 크기를 알 수 있어요.", "idx": 7, "translation": "Looking at photos from that time, you can see how big the dam is.", "vocab": [{"ko": "당시", "en": "that time, then, back then", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사진", "en": "photograph, photo", "note": ""}, {"ko": "크기", "en": "size", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~면", "exp": "Conditional: if/when you look at the photo, you can know the size.", "example_in_sentence": "보면"}, {"pattern": "~을/를 알 수 있어요", "exp": "To be able to know/understand something; expressing possibility.", "example_in_sentence": "크기를 알 수 있어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "사람들이 파이프 안에서 작아 보일 정도로 댐이 매우 커요.", "idx": 8, "translation": "The dam is so big that the people inside the pipe look small.", "vocab": [{"ko": "정도", "en": "degree, extent, level", "note": ""}, {"ko": "작다", "en": "to be small", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄹ 정도로", "exp": "To such a degree/extent that; expressing a high degree or intensity.", "example_in_sentence": "작아 보일 정도로"}, {"pattern": "~어 보이다", "exp": "To appear/seem to be in a certain state.", "example_in_sentence": "작아 보일"}], "analysis": []}], "version": "p2"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "후버댐", "en": "Hoover Dam", "note": "proper noun; a famous dam in the USA"}, {"ko": "만들다", "en": "to build, to make", "note": ""}, {"ko": "댐", "en": "dam", "note": ""}, {"ko": "물", "en": "water", "note": ""}, {"ko": "막다", "en": "to block, to stop", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전기", "en": "electricity", "note": ""}, {"ko": "공사 관계자", "en": "construction staff", "note": ""}, {"ko": "파이프", "en": "pipe", "note": ""}, {"ko": "타다", "en": "to ride; to get on", "note": ""}, {"ko": "통로", "en": "passage, channel, corridor", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지나가다", "en": "to pass through, to go by", "note": ""}, {"ko": "펜스톡", "en": "penstock", "note": "a type of pipe in a dam"}, {"ko": "부르다", "en": "to call, to name", "note": ""}, {"ko": "거의", "en": "almost, nearly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "완성되다", "en": "to be completed", "note": "passive/resultative form of 완성하다"}, {"ko": "지금", "en": "now", "note": ""}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전력", "en": "electric power, electricity", "note": ""}, {"ko": "당시", "en": "that time, then, back then", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사진", "en": "photograph, photo", "note": ""}, {"ko": "크기", "en": "size", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정도", "en": "degree, extent, level", "note": ""}, {"ko": "작다", "en": "to be small", "note": ""}, {"ko": "건물", "en": "building/structure", "note": "A large permanent structure; dam is a type of 건물"}, {"ko": "펜스톡 파이프", "en": "penstock pipe", "note": "Technical term; penstock = the pipe that carries water to turbines"}, {"ko": "지금도", "en": "even now/still today", "note": "Adverb emphasizing continuation to the present moment"}, {"ko": "알다", "en": "to know/understand", "note": "Here used in the sense ''to perceive'' or ''can tell''"}, {"ko": "작아 보이다", "en": "to appear/look small", "note": "~아 보이다 = to look/appear (a certain way); here describing visual perception"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": []}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moxvf48xqsi3' and md5(translation) = 'da1ed0c496abdcf734b92ded179d66d9';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Voyager 1 launched into space in 1977. It has been continuously flying for 47 years until now.", "This spacecraft moves at 38,000 miles per hour. That is 61,000 kilometers per hour. It''s really fast.", "As of 2026, Voyager 1 is now very far from Earth. It is as far as the distance light can travel in one day. This is called a \"light-day.\"", "Voyager 1 is still discovering new things in space right now. Scientists are receiving information sent by this spacecraft."], "sentences": [{"text": "보이저 1호(Voyager 1)는 1977년에 우주로 떠났어요.", "translation": "Voyager 1 launched into space in 1977.", "vocab": [{"ko": "보이저", "en": "Voyager (spacecraft name)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "우주", "en": "space / cosmos", "note": ""}, {"ko": "떠나다", "en": "to depart / to leave", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 떠나다 → 떠났어요 (left).", "example_in_sentence": "떠났어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (location/time)", "exp": "Static location or time marker. Marks when an action occurred. 1977년 (1977 year) + 에 = ''in 1977''.", "example_in_sentence": "1977년에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 (means/direction)", "exp": "Instrument, direction, or means particle. Marks destination or direction of movement. 우주 (space) + 로 = ''into space'' (direction of departure).", "example_in_sentence": "우주로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle attaching to noun. Marks the main topic of the sentence. 보이저 1호 + 는 = ''Voyager 1 (as for Voyager 1)''.", "example_in_sentence": "보이저 1호는"}]}, {"text": "지금까지 47년 동안 계속 날아가고 있어요.", "translation": "It has been continuously flying for 47 years until now.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지금까지", "en": "until now / so far", "note": ""}, {"ko": "동안", "en": "during / for (duration)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "계속", "en": "continuously / constantly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "날아가다", "en": "to fly away / to continue flying", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다 (continuous)", "exp": "Progressive aspect marker. Indicates ongoing or continuous action. 날아가다 (to fly) → 날아가 + 고 있어요 = ''is continuously flying'' or ''has been flying''.", "example_in_sentence": "날아가고 있어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~까지 (until)", "exp": "Temporal limit particle meaning ''up to / until''. 지금 (now) + 까지 = ''up to now / until now''.", "example_in_sentence": "지금까지"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~동안", "exp": "Duration marker. Expresses ''for [time period]'' or ''during [time period]''. 47년 (47 years) + 동안 = ''for 47 years''.", "example_in_sentence": "47년 동안"}]}, {"text": "이 우주선은 시속 38,000마일로 움직여요.", "translation": "This spacecraft moves at 38,000 miles per hour.", "vocab": [{"ko": "우주선", "en": "spacecraft", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시속", "en": "speed per hour", "note": ""}, {"ko": "마일", "en": "mile (unit of distance)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "움직이다", "en": "to move / to operate", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle. Marks the main subject being discussed. 우주선 (spacecraft) + 은 = ''this spacecraft (as for this spacecraft)''.", "example_in_sentence": "우주선은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 (means/direction)", "exp": "Means or manner particle. Indicates the rate or speed at which action occurs. 시속 38,000마일 (38,000 mph) + 로 = ''at 38,000 mph''.", "example_in_sentence": "시속 38,000마일로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어/여요 (present polite)", "exp": "Present polite informal ending. 움직이다 (to move) → 움직여요 = ''moves''.", "example_in_sentence": "움직여요"}]}, {"text": "이것은 시속 61,000킬로미터예요.", "translation": "That is 61,000 kilometers per hour.", "vocab": [{"ko": "킬로미터", "en": "kilometer (unit of distance)", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle. Marks the subject. 이것 (this/that) + 은 = ''this/that (as for this/that)''.", "example_in_sentence": "이것은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이에요/예요", "exp": "Polite ''to be''. 예요 is used after a noun ending in a vowel: 킬로미터 + 예요 = is … kilometers.", "example_in_sentence": "킬로미터예요"}]}, {"text": "정말 빨라요.", "translation": "It''s really fast.", "vocab": [{"ko": "정말", "en": "really / truly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "빠르다", "en": "to be fast / to be quick", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "르 irregular", "exp": "When a 르 stem meets 아/어, 르 becomes ㄹㄹ. 빠르다 → 빨라요 (is fast).", "example_in_sentence": "빨라요"}]}, {"text": "2026년 지금 보이저 1호는 지구에서 아주 멀리 있어요.", "translation": "As of 2026, Voyager 1 is now very far from Earth.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지구", "en": "Earth", "note": ""}, {"ko": "멀다", "en": "to be far / distant", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아주", "en": "very / extremely", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle. Marks the main subject. 보이저 1호 + 는 = ''Voyager 1 (as for Voyager 1)''.", "example_in_sentence": "보이저 1호는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (location/source)", "exp": "Locational or source particle. Marks the location or origin point. 지구 (Earth) + 에서 = ''from Earth'' (source of distance measurement).", "example_in_sentence": "지구에서"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~리 (adverb)", "exp": "멀다 (to be far) → 멀리 (far away), an adverb. 멀리 있어요 = is far away.", "example_in_sentence": "멀리 있어요"}]}, {"text": "빛이 하루 동안 갈 수 있는 거리만큼 멀어요.", "translation": "It is as far as the distance light can travel in one day.", "vocab": [{"ko": "빛", "en": "light", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하루", "en": "one day", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가다", "en": "to go / to travel", "note": ""}, {"ko": "거리", "en": "distance", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "exp": "Subject particle. Marks the grammatical subject of the clause. 빛 (light) + 이 = ''light (subject)''.", "example_in_sentence": "빛이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "Means ''can''. 가다 → 갈 수 있는 거리 (the distance it can travel).", "example_in_sentence": "갈 수 있는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~만큼 (degree/extent)", "exp": "Extent or degree particle meaning ''as much as / by the amount of''. 거리 (distance) + 만큼 = ''by the distance / as far as the distance''.", "example_in_sentence": "거리만큼"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~동안", "exp": "Duration marker. Expresses ''during / for [time period]''. 하루 (one day) + 동안 = ''during one day / in one day''.", "example_in_sentence": "하루 동안"}]}, {"text": "이것을 ''1광일(光日)''이라고 해요.", "translation": "This is called a \"light-day.\"", "vocab": [{"ko": "광일", "en": "light-day (distance light travels in one day)", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "Direct object particle. Marks the direct object of a transitive verb. 이것 (this) + 을 = ''this (direct object)''.", "example_in_sentence": "이것을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라고 하다", "exp": "Used to give a name: ''it is called…''. 1광일 + 이라고 해요 = it is called a light-day.", "example_in_sentence": "이라고 해요"}]}, {"text": "보이저 1호는 지금도 우주에서 새로운 것들을 발견하고 있어요.", "translation": "Voyager 1 is still discovering new things in space right now.", "vocab": [{"ko": "새롭다", "en": "to be new / to be fresh", "note": ""}, {"ko": "발견하다", "en": "to discover / to find", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle. Marks main subject. 보이저 1호 + 는 = ''Voyager 1 (as for Voyager 1)''.", "example_in_sentence": "보이저 1호는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~도 (also)", "exp": "Inclusive particle meaning ''also / too / even''. 지금 (now) + 도 = ''even now / still right now''.", "example_in_sentence": "지금도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (location/source)", "exp": "Locational particle marking where an action occurs. 우주 (space) + 에서 = ''in space''.", "example_in_sentence": "우주에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "ㅂ irregular + ~(으)ㄴ", "exp": "새롭다 is ㅂ-irregular: ㅂ becomes 우 before the modifier. 새롭다 → 새로운 (new).", "example_in_sentence": "새로운 것들"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "Direct object particle. 것들 (things) + 을 = ''things (direct object)''.", "example_in_sentence": "것들을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다 (continuous)", "exp": "Progressive aspect. 발견하다 (to discover) → 발견하 + 고 있어요 = ''is discovering / is in the process of discovering''.", "example_in_sentence": "발견하고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "과학자들은 이 우주선이 보내는 정보를 받고 있어요.", "translation": "Scientists are receiving information sent by this spacecraft.", "vocab": [{"ko": "과학자", "en": "scientist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보내다", "en": "to send", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정보", "en": "information", "note": ""}, {"ko": "받다", "en": "to receive / to accept", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "Topic particle. Marks the main subject. 과학자들 (scientists) + 은 = ''scientists (as for scientists)''.", "example_in_sentence": "과학자들은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "exp": "Subject particle for embedded clause. Marks the subject of a subordinate clause. 우주선 (spacecraft) + 이 = ''spacecraft (subject of embedded clause)''.", "example_in_sentence": "우주선이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present modifier)", "exp": "Verb form used before a noun for something happening now. 보내다 → 보내는 정보 (the information it sends).", "example_in_sentence": "보내는 정보"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "Direct object particle. 정보 (information) + 를 = ''information (direct object)''.", "example_in_sentence": "정보를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다 (continuous)", "exp": "Progressive aspect. 받다 (to receive) → stem 받 + 고 있어요 = ''is receiving / are in the process of receiving''.", "example_in_sentence": "받고 있어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "보이저", "en": "Voyager (spacecraft name)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "우주", "en": "space / cosmos", "note": ""}, {"ko": "떠나다", "en": "to depart / to leave", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지금까지", "en": "until now / so far", "note": ""}, {"ko": "동안", "en": "during / for (duration)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "계속", "en": "continuously / constantly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "날아가다", "en": "to fly away / to continue flying", "note": ""}, {"ko": "우주선", "en": "spacecraft", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시속", "en": "speed per hour", "note": ""}, {"ko": "마일", "en": "mile (unit of distance)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "움직이다", "en": "to move / to operate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "킬로미터", "en": "kilometer (unit of distance)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정말", "en": "really / truly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "빠르다", "en": "to be fast / to be quick", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지구", "en": "Earth", "note": ""}, {"ko": "멀다", "en": "to be far / distant", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아주", "en": "very / extremely", "note": ""}, {"ko": "빛", "en": "light", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하루", "en": "one day", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가다", "en": "to go / to travel", "note": ""}, {"ko": "거리", "en": "distance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "광일", "en": "light-day (distance light travels in one day)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "새롭다", "en": "to be new / to be fresh", "note": ""}, {"ko": "발견하다", "en": "to discover / to find", "note": ""}, {"ko": "과학자", "en": "scientist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보내다", "en": "to send", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정보", "en": "information", "note": ""}, {"ko": "받다", "en": "to receive / to accept", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~았/었어요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Past tense polite ending. 떠나다 → 떠났어요 (left).", "ex_ko": "보이저 1호(Voyager 1)는 1977년에 우주로 떠났어요.", "ex_en": "Voyager 1 launched into space in 1977."}, {"name": "~에서 (location/source)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Locational or source particle. Marks the location or origin point. 지구 (Earth) + 에서 = ''from Earth'' (source of distance measurement).", "ex_ko": "보이저 1호(Voyager 1)는 1977년에 우주로 떠났어요.", "ex_en": "Voyager 1 launched into space in 1977."}, {"name": "~(으)로 (means/direction)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Instrument, direction, or means particle. Marks destination or direction of movement. 우주 (space) + 로 = ''into space'' (direction of departure).", "ex_ko": "보이저 1호(Voyager 1)는 1977년에 우주로 떠났어요.", "ex_en": "Voyager 1 launched into space in 1977."}, {"name": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Topic particle. Marks the main subject being discussed. 우주선 (spacecraft) + 은 = ''this spacecraft (as for this spacecraft)''.", "ex_ko": "보이저 1호(Voyager 1)는 1977년에 우주로 떠났어요.", "ex_en": "Voyager 1 launched into space in 1977."}, {"name": "~고 있다 (continuous)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Progressive aspect marker. Indicates ongoing or continuous action. 날아가다 (to fly) → 날아가 + 고 있어요 = ''is continuously flying'' or ''has been flying''.", "ex_ko": "지금까지 47년 동안 계속 날아가고 있어요.", "ex_en": "It has been continuously flying for 47 years until now."}, {"name": "~까지 (until)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Temporal limit particle meaning ''up to / until''. 지금 (now) + 까지 = ''up to now / until now''.", "ex_ko": "지금까지 47년 동안 계속 날아가고 있어요.", "ex_en": "It has been continuously flying for 47 years until now."}, {"name": "~아/어/여요 (present polite)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Present polite informal ending. 움직이다 (to move) → 움직여요 = ''moves''.", "ex_ko": "이 우주선은 시속 38,000마일로 움직여요.", "ex_en": "This spacecraft moves at 38,000 miles per hour."}, {"name": "~이에요/예요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Polite ''to be''. 예요 is used after a noun ending in a vowel: 킬로미터 + 예요 = is … kilometers.", "ex_ko": "이것은 시속 61,000킬로미터예요.", "ex_en": "That is 61,000 kilometers per hour."}, {"name": "르 irregular", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "When a 르 stem meets 아/어, 르 becomes ㄹㄹ. 빠르다 → 빨라요 (is fast).", "ex_ko": "정말 빨라요.", "ex_en": "It''s really fast."}, {"name": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Subject particle for embedded clause. Marks the subject of a subordinate clause. 우주선 (spacecraft) + 이 = ''spacecraft (subject of embedded clause)''.", "ex_ko": "빛이 하루 동안 갈 수 있는 거리만큼 멀어요.", "ex_en": "It is as far as the distance light can travel in one day."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''can''. 가다 → 갈 수 있는 거리 (the distance it can travel).", "ex_ko": "빛이 하루 동안 갈 수 있는 거리만큼 멀어요.", "ex_en": "It is as far as the distance light can travel in one day."}, {"name": "~만큼 (degree/extent)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Extent or degree particle meaning ''as much as / by the amount of''. 거리 (distance) + 만큼 = ''by the distance / as far as the distance''.", "ex_ko": "빛이 하루 동안 갈 수 있는 거리만큼 멀어요.", "ex_en": "It is as far as the distance light can travel in one day."}, {"name": "~을/를 (object marker)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Direct object particle. Marks the direct object of a transitive verb. 이것 (this) + 을 = ''this (direct object)''.", "ex_ko": "이것을 ''1광일(光日)''이라고 해요.", "ex_en": "This is called a \"light-day.\""}, {"name": "~(이)라고 하다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Used to give a name: ''it is called…''. 1광일 + 이라고 해요 = it is called a light-day.", "ex_ko": "이것을 ''1광일(光日)''이라고 해요.", "ex_en": "This is called a \"light-day.\""}, {"name": "~도 (also)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Inclusive particle meaning ''also / too / even''. 지금 (now) + 도 = ''even now / still right now''.", "ex_ko": "보이저 1호는 지금도 우주에서 새로운 것들을 발견하고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Voyager 1 is still discovering new things in space right now."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moyxs1tnbrs5' and md5(translation) = '98f3212a16a2522292229886862000c0';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["An enormous lithium deposit has been discovered in the United States. The value of this lithium is estimated at approximately 1.5 trillion dollars. In Korean currency, this amounts to about 1,600 trillion won.", "Lithium is an essential material for making electric vehicle batteries and smartphone batteries. As the electric vehicle market has been growing rapidly in recent years, the importance of lithium is increasing even more. Korean companies Samsung and LG are also significantly expanding their battery businesses.", "Until now, lithium has been produced mainly in South America and Australia. The discovery of such a large-scale deposit in the United States is very rare. This discovery is expected to bring major changes to the global lithium supply.", "Experts say this discovery will have a significant impact on the electric vehicle and battery industries. If lithium prices become stabilized, electric vehicle prices could become more affordable. This seems like it could be a good opportunity for Korean companies as well."], "sentences": [{"text": "미국에서 엄청난 규모의 리튬 매장량이 발견되었어요.", "translation": "An enormous lithium deposit has been discovered in the United States.", "vocab": [{"ko": "엄청나다", "en": "to be enormous/tremendous", "note": "Colloquial intensifier; common in spoken Korean for emphasis"}, {"ko": "매장량", "en": "deposit amount/reserve quantity", "note": "Compound: 매장 (deposit) + 량 (quantity)"}, {"ko": "발견되다", "en": "to be discovered/found", "note": "Passive voice of 발견하다"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~(으)ㄴ 규모의 N", "exp": "Describes a noun by modifying it with a descriptive clause; the modifier agrees in definiteness with the head noun.", "example_in_sentence": "엄청난 규모의 리튬 매장량"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 리튬의 가치는 약 1조 5천억 달러로 추정돼요.", "translation": "The value of this lithium is estimated at approximately 1.5 trillion dollars.", "vocab": [{"ko": "가치", "en": "value/worth", "note": "Abstract noun; often paired with 있다 or in estimation contexts"}, {"ko": "추정되다", "en": "to be estimated", "note": "Passive; subject is the thing being estimated"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "한국 돈으로는 약 1600조원에 달하는 금액이에요.", "translation": "In Korean currency, this amounts to about 1,600 trillion won.", "vocab": [{"ko": "달하다", "en": "to amount to/reach", "note": "Formal; expresses numerical totals or quantities"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "리튬은 전기차 배터리와 스마트폰 배터리를 만드는 데 꼭 필요한 재료예요.", "translation": "Lithium is an essential material for making electric vehicle batteries and smartphone batteries.", "vocab": [{"ko": "꼭", "en": "surely; absolutely", "note": "Adverb emphasizing necessity; often modifies 필요하다"}, {"ko": "필요하다", "en": "to be necessary/needed", "note": "Common predicate; can take ~하다 or be used as adjective form ~한"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "최근 전기차 시장이 빠르게 성장하면서 리튬의 중요성도 더욱 커지고 있어요.", "translation": "As the electric vehicle market has been growing rapidly in recent years, the importance of lithium is increasing even more.", "vocab": [{"ko": "중요성", "en": "importance", "note": "Abstract noun; nominalization of 중요하다"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~(으)면서", "exp": "Connects two actions or states that occur simultaneously or as parallel consequences; the subject typically remains the same.", "example_in_sentence": "빠르게 성장하면서 리튬의 중요성도 더욱 커지고 있어요"}, {"pattern": "~고 있다", "exp": "Indicates an ongoing or progressive action/state; the process is in motion.", "example_in_sentence": "커지고 있어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "한국의 삼성과 엘지도 배터리 사업을 크게 확장하고 있는 상황이에요.", "translation": "Korean companies Samsung and LG are also significantly expanding their battery businesses.", "vocab": [{"ko": "확장하다", "en": "to expand/extend", "note": "Formal verb; often used in business/institutional contexts"}, {"ko": "상황", "en": "situation/state of affairs", "note": "Marks a descriptive state or circumstance"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~고 있는 상황", "exp": "Describes an ongoing situation or process; emphasizes the continuity and current state.", "example_in_sentence": "배터리 사업을 크게 확장하고 있는 상황"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "지금까지 리튬은 주로 남미와 호주에서 생산되었어요.", "translation": "Until now, lithium has been produced mainly in South America and Australia.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지금까지", "en": "until now/so far", "note": "Temporal adverb marking the period up to the present"}, {"ko": "주로", "en": "mainly/primarily", "note": "Adverb of degree; modifies how an action is distributed"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "미국에서 이런 대규모 매장량이 발견된 것은 매우 드문 일이에요.", "translation": "The discovery of such a large-scale deposit in the United States is very rare.", "vocab": [{"ko": "드물다", "en": "to be rare/uncommon", "note": "Adjective; opposite of 흔하다 (common)"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ 것은", "exp": "Nominalizes a clause and highlights it as the topic; shifts focus to the event or fact itself.", "example_in_sentence": "발견된 것은 매우 드문 일이에요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 발견으로 전 세계 리튬 공급에 큰 변화가 생길 것으로 예상돼요.", "translation": "This discovery is expected to bring major changes to the global lithium supply.", "vocab": [{"ko": "예상되다", "en": "to be expected/anticipated", "note": "Passive; subject is what is foreseen"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄹ 것으로 예상되다", "exp": "Expresses passive expectation or prediction; the future event is anticipated by an external observer or general consensus.", "example_in_sentence": "생길 것으로 예상돼요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "전문가들은 이번 발견이 전기차와 배터리 산업에 큰 영향을 줄 것이라고 말해요.", "translation": "Experts say this discovery will have a significant impact on the electric vehicle and battery industries.", "vocab": [{"ko": "영향", "en": "impact/influence", "note": "Noun; commonly paired with ~을 주다 (to exert impact)"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄹ 것이라고 말하다", "exp": "Reports someone''s prediction or assertion about a future event; standard indirect speech pattern.", "example_in_sentence": "큰 영향을 줄 것이라고 말해요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "리튬 가격이 안정되면 전기차 가격도 더 저렴해질 수 있어요.", "translation": "If lithium prices stabilize, electric car prices could also get cheaper.", "vocab": [{"ko": "안정되다", "en": "to become stable/stabilized", "note": "Passive change of state; indicates transition to stability"}, {"ko": "저렴해지다", "en": "to become cheaper/more affordable", "note": "Change-of-state verb; 저렴하다 (cheap/affordable) + ~아/어지다"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~(으)면", "exp": "Conditional ending; presents a hypothetical scenario and its potential consequence.", "example_in_sentence": "가격이 안정되면"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "한국 기업들에게도 좋은 기회가 될 것 같아요.", "translation": "This seems like it could be a good opportunity for Korean companies as well.", "vocab": [{"ko": "기회", "en": "opportunity/chance", "note": "Noun; often paired with 갖다 or descriptive modifiers like 좋은"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄹ 것 같다", "exp": "Expresses conjecture or probability; softens the statement to indicate likelihood rather than certainty.", "example_in_sentence": "좋은 기회가 될 것 같아요"}], "analysis": []}], "version": "p5"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "엄청나다", "en": "to be enormous/tremendous", "note": "Colloquial intensifier; common in spoken Korean for emphasis"}, {"ko": "매장량", "en": "deposit amount/reserve quantity", "note": "Compound: 매장 (deposit) + 량 (quantity)"}, {"ko": "발견되다", "en": "to be discovered/found", "note": "Passive voice of 발견하다"}, {"ko": "가치", "en": "value/worth", "note": "Abstract noun; often paired with 있다 or in estimation contexts"}, {"ko": "추정되다", "en": "to be estimated", "note": "Passive; subject is the thing being estimated"}, {"ko": "달하다", "en": "to amount to/reach", "note": "Formal; expresses numerical totals or quantities"}, {"ko": "꼭", "en": "surely; absolutely", "note": "Adverb emphasizing necessity; often modifies 필요하다"}, {"ko": "필요하다", "en": "to be necessary/needed", "note": "Common predicate; can take ~하다 or be used as adjective form ~한"}, {"ko": "중요성", "en": "importance", "note": "Abstract noun; nominalization of 중요하다"}, {"ko": "확장하다", "en": "to expand/extend", "note": "Formal verb; often used in business/institutional contexts"}, {"ko": "상황", "en": "situation/state of affairs", "note": "Marks a descriptive state or circumstance"}, {"ko": "지금까지", "en": "until now/so far", "note": "Temporal adverb marking the period up to the present"}, {"ko": "주로", "en": "mainly/primarily", "note": "Adverb of degree; modifies how an action is distributed"}, {"ko": "드물다", "en": "to be rare/uncommon", "note": "Adjective; opposite of 흔하다 (common)"}, {"ko": "예상되다", "en": "to be expected/anticipated", "note": "Passive; subject is what is foreseen"}, {"ko": "영향", "en": "impact/influence", "note": "Noun; commonly paired with ~을 주다 (to exert impact)"}, {"ko": "안정되다", "en": "to become stable/stabilized", "note": "Passive change of state; indicates transition to stability"}, {"ko": "저렴해지다", "en": "to become cheaper/more affordable", "note": "Change-of-state verb; 저렴하다 (cheap/affordable) + ~아/어지다"}, {"ko": "기회", "en": "opportunity/chance", "note": "Noun; often paired with 갖다 or descriptive modifiers like 좋은"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": []}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moyxss2onp4u' and md5(translation) = '73fff9b201f992c39c14faaa7dbf9144';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["How much food can you buy with the price of a pack of cigarettes in Australia? A photo that recently went viral online is answering this question.", "Australia is one of the countries with the most expensive cigarette prices in the world. A pack of cigarettes costs around 40,000 to 50,000 won. With this money, you can buy various groceries such as bread, milk, fruits, and vegetables.", "Looking at the photo, you can see that with the price of one pack of cigarettes, a family can buy enough food to eat for a day. Many people are gaining a new awareness of the economic burden of cigarettes after seeing this comparison.", "Cigarette prices in Korea are also continuing to rise. It would be good to consider quitting smoking from both health and economic perspectives."], "sentences": [{"text": "호주에서 담배 한 갑 가격으로 얼마나 많은 음식을 살 수 있을까요?", "translation": "How much food can you buy with the price of a pack of cigarettes in Australia?", "vocab": [{"ko": "담배", "en": "cigarette", "note": ""}, {"ko": "갑", "en": "pack (counter)", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로", "exp": "Marks the means: ''with''. 가격으로 = with the price (of).", "example_in_sentence": "가격으로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "Means ''can''. 사다 (to buy) → 살 수 있다 (can buy).", "example_in_sentence": "살 수 있을까요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ까요", "exp": "Question ending for wondering: ''I wonder…?''. 있다 → 있을까요?", "example_in_sentence": "있을까요"}]}, {"text": "최근 온라인에서 화제가 된 사진이 이 질문에 답을 주고 있어요.", "translation": "A photo that recently went viral online is answering this question.", "vocab": [{"ko": "화제", "en": "hot topic", "note": "화제가 되다 = become a hot topic"}, {"ko": "답을 주다", "en": "to answer, provide an answer", "note": "답 (answer) + 을 (object) + 주다 (to give)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "continuous/progressive aspect. Is V-ing. 주고 있어요 = is giving/answering", "example_in_sentence": "주고 있어요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "화제가 되다", "exp": "to become a hot topic, go viral. 사진이 화제가 된 = photo that became viral", "example_in_sentence": "화제가 된"}]}, {"text": "호주는 세계에서 담배값이 가장 비싼 나라 중 하나예요.", "translation": "Australia is one of the countries with the most expensive cigarette prices in the world.", "vocab": [{"ko": "담배값", "en": "cigarette price", "note": "담배 (cigarette) + 값 (price)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ 중 하나", "exp": "Means ''one of''. 비싼 나라 중 하나 = one of the most expensive countries.", "example_in_sentence": "나라 중 하나"}]}, {"text": "담배 한 갑 가격이 약 4만 원에서 5만 원 정도 한다고 해요.", "translation": "A pack of cigarettes costs around 40,000 to 50,000 won, they say.", "vocab": [{"ko": "정도", "en": "approximately, about, roughly", "note": "expressing approximation or degree"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "A에서 B", "exp": "Shows a range: ''from A to B''. 4만 원에서 5만 원 = from 40,000 to 50,000 won.", "example_in_sentence": "4만 원에서 5만 원"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다고 하다", "exp": "Reports what others say: ''they say that…''. 하다 → 한다고 해요 (they say it costs).", "example_in_sentence": "한다고 해요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~ 정도 하다", "exp": "Gives an approximate price: ''costs about…''. 5만 원 정도 한다 = it costs about 50,000 won.", "example_in_sentence": "정도 한다고"}]}, {"text": "이 돈으로는 빵, 우유, 과일, 채소 등 다양한 식료품을 살 수 있어요.", "translation": "With this money, you can buy various groceries such as bread, milk, fruits, and vegetables.", "vocab": [{"ko": "식료품", "en": "groceries, food items", "note": "식료 (food) + 품 (goods)"}, {"ko": "다양하다", "en": "to be various; diverse", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다/없다", "exp": "ability/possibility. Can V. 살 수 있어요 = can buy", "example_in_sentence": "살 수 있어요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~으로는", "exp": "with/by (means) emphatic; 이 돈으로는 = with this money (implying scope or limitation)", "example_in_sentence": "돈으로는"}]}, {"text": "사진을 보면 담배 한 갑값으로 가족이 하루 먹을 수 있는 충분한 음식을 살 수 있다는 것을 알 수 있어요.", "translation": "Looking at the photo, you can see that with the price of one pack of cigarettes, a family can buy enough food to eat for a day.", "vocab": [{"ko": "충분하다", "en": "to be enough; sufficient", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면", "exp": "conditional. If/when. 보면 = if you look/when you look", "example_in_sentence": "보면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "Means ''can''. 먹다 → 먹을 수 있는 음식 (food one can eat).", "example_in_sentence": "먹을 수 있는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로", "exp": "means/direction/instrument. With/by. 갑값으로 = with the pack price", "example_in_sentence": "갑값으로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다는 것을 알다", "exp": "Means ''to see/realize that…''. 살 수 있다 → 살 수 있다는 것을 알 수 있어요 (you can see that one can buy…).", "example_in_sentence": "살 수 있다는 것을"}]}, {"text": "많은 사람들이 이 비교를 보고 담배의 경제적 부담을 새롭게 깨닫고 있다고 해요.", "translation": "Many people are gaining a new awareness of the economic burden of cigarettes after seeing this comparison.", "vocab": [{"ko": "비교", "en": "comparison", "note": ""}, {"ko": "부담", "en": "burden, load", "note": ""}, {"ko": "깨닫다", "en": "to realize, become aware", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "continuous/progressive aspect. Is V-ing. 깨닫고 있다 = are realizing, are gaining awareness", "example_in_sentence": "깨닫고 있다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게", "exp": "adverbializer suffix. Forms adverbs from adjectives. 새롭다 (new) → 새롭게 (newly/in a new way)", "example_in_sentence": "새롭게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다고 하다", "exp": "Reports what others say: ''it is said that…''. 있다 → 있다고 해요.", "example_in_sentence": "있다고 해요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~을/를 보고", "exp": "보다 → 보고: ''after seeing''. 비교를 보고 = after seeing the comparison.", "example_in_sentence": "비교를 보고"}]}, {"text": "한국도 담배값이 계속 오르고 있어요.", "translation": "Cigarette prices in Korea are also continuing to rise.", "vocab": [{"ko": "계속", "en": "continuously, keep on, continue", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "continuous/progressive aspect. Is V-ing. 오르고 있어요 = is rising, continues to rise", "example_in_sentence": "오르고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "건강과 경제적 측면에서 금연을 고려해 보는 것이 좋겠어요.", "translation": "It would be good to consider quitting smoking from both health and economic perspectives.", "vocab": [{"ko": "측면", "en": "aspect, perspective, viewpoint", "note": ""}, {"ko": "금연", "en": "smoking cessation, quitting smoking", "note": "금 (abstain) + 연 (smoking)"}, {"ko": "고려하다", "en": "to consider, take into account", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "Here 에서 means ''in terms of''. 측면에서 = from the … point of view.", "example_in_sentence": "측면에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 보다", "exp": "Means ''try doing''. 고려하다 → 고려해 보다 (to give it some thought).", "example_in_sentence": "고려해 보는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~겠", "exp": "intention/conjecture/future. 좋겠어요 = it would be good (polite conjecture/recommendation)", "example_in_sentence": "좋겠어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것이 좋겠다", "exp": "Gives soft advice: ''it would be good to…''. 고려해 보다 → 고려해 보는 것이 좋겠어요.", "example_in_sentence": "고려해 보는 것이 좋겠어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "담배", "en": "cigarette", "note": ""}, {"ko": "갑", "en": "pack (counter)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "화제", "en": "hot topic", "note": "화제가 되다 = become a hot topic"}, {"ko": "답을 주다", "en": "to answer, provide an answer", "note": "답 (answer) + 을 (object) + 주다 (to give)"}, {"ko": "담배값", "en": "cigarette price", "note": "담배 (cigarette) + 값 (price)"}, {"ko": "정도", "en": "approximately, about, roughly", "note": "expressing approximation or degree"}, {"ko": "식료품", "en": "groceries, food items", "note": "식료 (food) + 품 (goods)"}, {"ko": "다양하다", "en": "to be various; diverse", "note": ""}, {"ko": "충분하다", "en": "to be enough; sufficient", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비교", "en": "comparison", "note": ""}, {"ko": "부담", "en": "burden, load", 