"auxiliary: to try doing; to attempt", "ex_ko": "손을 천천히 내밀어서 냄새를 맡아봤어요.", "ex_en": "It slowly extended its hand and tried to smell it."}, {"name": "~지 않다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "negation marker; did not", "ex_ko": "강아지도 무서워하지 않고 가만히 있었어요.", "ex_en": "The puppy also did not get scared and stayed still."}, {"name": "~고", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Links two actions: ''and''. 않다 → 않고. 무서워하지 않고 = without being scared, and…", "ex_ko": "강아지도 무서워하지 않고 가만히 있었어요.", "ex_en": "The puppy also did not get scared and stayed still."}, {"name": "~도", "level": "Starter", "exp": "particle: also; too; even", "ex_ko": "강아지도 무서워하지 않고 가만히 있었어요.", "ex_en": "The puppy also did not get scared and stayed still."}, {"name": "~이/가 되다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Means ''to become''. 친구 + 가 되었어요 = became friends.", "ex_ko": "두 동물은 서로 친구가 되었어요.", "ex_en": "The two animals became friends with each other."}, {"name": "두 + noun", "level": "Starter", "exp": "둘 (two) becomes 두 before a noun. 두 동물 = two animals.", "ex_ko": "두 동물은 서로 친구가 되었어요.", "ex_en": "The two animals became friends with each other."}, {"name": "~아/어 주다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "auxiliary: to do for (recipient); favor/benefit sense", "ex_ko": "침팬지는 강아지를 부드럽게 만져주었어요.", "ex_en": "The chimpanzee gently touched the puppy."}, {"name": "~는 (present modifier)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Verb form used before a noun. 만나다 → 만나는 친구 (a friend they meet).", "ex_ko": "동물들도 처음 만나는 친구에게 관심을 보여요.", "ex_en": "Animals also show interest in friends they meet for the first time."}, {"name": "~지만", "level": "Starter", "exp": "connective: but; however; despite; contrast", "ex_ko": "서로 다른 동물이지만 잘 지낼 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "Even though they are different animals, they can get along well."}, {"name": "~ㄹ/을 수 있다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "auxiliary: can; able to; possibility", "ex_ko": "서로 다른 동물이지만 잘 지낼 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "Even though they are different animals, they can get along well."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moyxu9upch6a' and md5(translation) = '65cfd110a609f70905e9272bf8606778';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["There is old footage taken in 1919 and 1920. It shows soldiers who participated in World War I.", "These soldiers suffered severe psychological wounds because of the war. Even though the war had ended, they were still struggling.", "The soldiers displayed various symptoms. They became frightened when they saw war-related objects or military uniforms. Their bodies would shake or they would have convulsions.", "Some soldiers suddenly engaged in military training behaviors. Even though the war had ended, they continued to act as if the war was still ongoing.", "This footage shows how deeply war wounds people. Even now, a hundred years later, many people remain interested in this issue."], "sentences": [{"text": "1919년과 1920년에 찍은 오래된 영상이 있어요.", "translation": "There is old footage taken in 1919 and 1920.", "vocab": [{"ko": "찍다", "en": "to take (a photo/video)", "note": "Common for capturing images or film"}, {"ko": "오래되다", "en": "to be old", "note": "Describes age of objects; 오래된 = old (adjective form)"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "A past participle form used to modify a noun; describes the noun''s completed state or origin.", "example_in_sentence": "찍은 오래된 영상"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "제1차 세계대전에 참전했던 군인들의 모습이에요.", "translation": "It shows soldiers who participated in World War I.", "vocab": [{"ko": "참전하다", "en": "to participate in war", "note": "Formal verb combining 참 (participate) + 전 (war)"}, {"ko": "모습", "en": "appearance; figure; sight", "note": "What something or someone looks like; often used with 보이다"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~았던 (past participle modifier)", "exp": "Marks a completed past action used to modify the following noun; emphasizes the action happened in the past.", "example_in_sentence": "참전했던 군인들"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 군인들은 전쟁 때문에 마음에 큰 상처를 받았어요.", "translation": "These soldiers suffered severe psychological wounds because of the war.", "vocab": [{"ko": "상처", "en": "wound; injury; trauma", "note": "Can be physical or psychological"}, {"ko": "받다", "en": "to receive; to suffer", "note": "상처를 받다 = to be wounded/suffer trauma"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "전쟁이 끝났지만 아직도 힘들어했어요.", "translation": "Even though the war had ended, they were still struggling.", "vocab": [{"ko": "끝나다", "en": "to end; to finish", "note": "Intransitive verb; past form 끝났어요"}, {"ko": "힘들어하다", "en": "to have a hard time; to struggle", "note": "과거 형태: 힘들어했어요"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~(었)지만", "exp": "Conjunction expressing contrast; connects two clauses where the second contradicts or opposes the first.", "example_in_sentence": "전쟁이 끝났지만"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "군인들은 여러 가지 증상을 보였어요.", "translation": "The soldiers displayed various symptoms.", "vocab": [{"ko": "여러 가지", "en": "various; several kinds of", "note": "여러 = several; 가지 = kind/type"}, {"ko": "증상", "en": "symptom", "note": "Medical/psychological term"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "전쟁과 관련된 물건이나 군복을 보면 무서워했어요.", "translation": "They became frightened when they saw war-related objects or military uniforms.", "vocab": [{"ko": "관련되다", "en": "to be related to", "note": "전쟁과 관련된 = war-related"}, {"ko": "군복", "en": "military uniform", "note": "군 (military) + 복 (clothes)"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~(으)면", "exp": "Conditional ending: ''if/when [condition], then [result]''; marks the triggering condition.", "example_in_sentence": "보면 무서워했어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "몸이 떨리거나 경련을 일으키기도 했어요.", "translation": "Their bodies would shake or they would have convulsions.", "vocab": [{"ko": "떨리다", "en": "to shake; to tremble", "note": "Involuntary shaking of the body"}, {"ko": "경련", "en": "convulsion; spasm", "note": "Medical term for involuntary muscle contractions"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~거나", "exp": "Conjunction expressing alternatives or listing options; ''or; either...or''.", "example_in_sentence": "떨리거나 경련을 일으키기도"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "어떤 군인들은 갑자기 군사 훈련을 하는 행동을 했어요.", "translation": "Some soldiers suddenly acted as if they were doing military drills.", "vocab": [{"ko": "갑자기", "en": "suddenly; abruptly", "note": "Adverb describing unexpected or immediate action"}, {"ko": "훈련", "en": "training; drill", "note": "군사 훈련 = military training"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}, {"text": "전쟁이 끝났는데도 계속 전쟁 중인 것처럼 행동했어요.", "translation": "Even though the war had ended, they continued to act as if the war was still ongoing.", "vocab": [{"ko": "계속", "en": "continuously; still", "note": "Often used with ~(으)면서 or infinitive form"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~(으)면서", "exp": "Conjunction showing simultaneous or contrasting actions; ''while; even as; yet''.", "example_in_sentence": "전쟁이 끝났는데도 계속"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 영상은 전쟁이 사람들에게 얼마나 큰 상처를 주는지 보여줘요.", "translation": "This footage shows how deeply war wounds people.", "vocab": [{"ko": "보여주다", "en": "to show; to demonstrate", "note": "보이다 + 주다 = show to someone"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~얼마나 (어떻게)", "exp": "Interrogative adverb in indirect question construction; ''how much/how deeply/to what extent''.", "example_in_sentence": "얼마나 큰 상처를 주는지 보여줘요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "100년이 지난 지금도 많은 사람들이 이 문제에 관심을 가지고 있어요.", "translation": "Even now, a hundred years later, many people remain interested in this issue.", "vocab": [{"ko": "지나다", "en": "to pass; to go by", "note": "100년이 지난 = a hundred years have passed"}, {"ko": "관심", "en": "interest; concern", "note": "관심을 가지다 = to take/show interest"}], "grammar": [], "analysis": []}], "version": "p5"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "찍다", "en": "to take (a photo/video)", "note": "Common for capturing images or film"}, {"ko": "오래되다", "en": "to be old", "note": "Describes age of objects; 오래된 = old (adjective form)"}, {"ko": "참전하다", "en": "to participate in war", "note": "Formal verb combining 참 (participate) + 전 (war)"}, {"ko": "모습", "en": "appearance; figure; sight", "note": "What something or someone looks like; often used with 보이다"}, {"ko": "상처", "en": "wound; injury; trauma", "note": "Can be physical or psychological"}, {"ko": "받다", "en": "to receive; to suffer", "note": "상처를 받다 = to be wounded/suffer trauma"}, {"ko": "끝나다", "en": "to end; to finish", "note": "Intransitive verb; past form 끝났어요"}, {"ko": "힘들어하다", "en": "to have a hard time; to struggle", "note": "과거 형태: 힘들어했어요"}, {"ko": "여러 가지", "en": "various; several kinds of", "note": "여러 = several; 가지 = kind/type"}, {"ko": "증상", "en": "symptom", "note": "Medical/psychological term"}, {"ko": "관련되다", "en": "to be related to", "note": "전쟁과 관련된 = war-related"}, {"ko": "군복", "en": "military uniform", "note": "군 (military) + 복 (clothes)"}, {"ko": "떨리다", "en": "to shake; to tremble", "note": "Involuntary shaking of the body"}, {"ko": "경련", "en": "convulsion; spasm", "note": "Medical term for involuntary muscle contractions"}, {"ko": "갑자기", "en": "suddenly; abruptly", "note": "Adverb describing unexpected or immediate action"}, {"ko": "훈련", "en": "training; drill", "note": "군사 훈련 = military training"}, {"ko": "계속", "en": "continuously; still", "note": "Often used with ~(으)면서 or infinitive form"}, {"ko": "보여주다", "en": "to show; to demonstrate", "note": "보이다 + 주다 = show to someone"}, {"ko": "지나다", "en": "to pass; to go by", "note": "100년이 지난 = a hundred years have passed"}, {"ko": "관심", "en": "interest; concern", "note": "관심을 가지다 = to take/show interest"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": []}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moyxv0qwk2mb' and md5(translation) = 'bed97b340f21ecc886de4158adc4243e';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Former U.S. President Jimmy Carter was diagnosed with brain cancer in 2015. In 2019, he injured his hip bone. That same year, at the age of 95, he fell at home and needed 14 stitches. However, the very next day, he participated in a Habitat for Humanity volunteer activity. Habitat is an organization that builds houses for people without homes. Former President Carter helped with house building despite his injury. Many people were moved by his actions. I think it''s admirable how he serves others for the sake of helping people, even at an advanced age and despite being in pain.", "Korean Teacher Shortage Becomes Serious, School Classes Disrupted", "What is an \"anxiety bag\"? A Popular Trend", "The United States and China Resume Talks Over Trade Issues", "\"Talking Pig\" Becomes SNS Star", "Apple Greatly Improves iPhone Speed with New AI Chip"], "sentences": [{"text": "지미 카터 전 미국 대통령은 2015년에 뇌암에 걸렸어요.", "translation": "Former U.S. President Jimmy Carter contracted brain cancer in 2015.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전", "en": "former"}, {"ko": "뇌암", "en": "brain cancer"}, {"ko": "걸리다", "en": "to contract (disease)"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "2019년에는 엉덩이뼈를 다쳤어요.", "translation": "In 2019, he injured his hip bone.", "vocab": [{"ko": "엉덩이뼈", "en": "hip bone"}, {"ko": "다치다", "en": "to be injured"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "같은 해 95세의 나이에 집에서 넘어져서 14바늘을 꿰매야 했어요.", "translation": "That same year, at the age of 95, he fell at home and had to get 14 stitches.", "vocab": [{"ko": "같다", "en": "to be the same"}, {"ko": "넘어지다", "en": "to fall"}, {"ko": "꿰매다", "en": "to stitch"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~어서", "exp": "Connective ending indicating sequential or causal relationship. 넘어지다 → 넘어져서, showing that falling caused the need for stitches.", "example_in_sentence": "넘어져서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어야 하다", "exp": "Auxiliary construction expressing obligation or necessity. 꿰매다 → 꿰매야 하다, meaning ''had to stitch.''", "example_in_sentence": "꿰매야 했어요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 다음 날 바로 해비타트(Habitat for Humanity) 봉사활동에 참여했어요.", "translation": "However, the very next day he participated in Habitat for Humanity volunteer work.", "vocab": [{"ko": "하지만", "en": "but, however"}, {"ko": "바로", "en": "immediately, right"}, {"ko": "참여하다", "en": "to participate"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "해비타트는 집이 없는 사람들을 위해 집을 짓는 단체예요.", "translation": "Habitat is an organization that builds houses for people who do not have homes.", "vocab": [{"ko": "집", "en": "house"}, {"ko": "짓다", "en": "to build"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present modifier)", "exp": "Verb form used before a noun. 짓다 → 짓는 단체 (an organization that builds).", "example_in_sentence": "짓는 단체"}]}, {"text": "카터 전 대통령은 부상에도 불구하고 집짓기를 도왔어요.", "translation": "Former President Carter helped with house building despite the injury.", "vocab": [{"ko": "부상", "en": "injury"}, {"ko": "돕다", "en": "to help"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~에도 불구하고", "exp": "Expression meaning ''in spite of'' or ''despite.'' Shows that the action occurred regardless of the obstacle.", "example_in_sentence": "부상에도 불구하고"}]}, {"text": "많은 사람들이 그의 행동을 보고 감동했어요.", "translation": "Many people saw his actions and were moved.", "vocab": [{"ko": "행동", "en": "action, behavior"}, {"ko": "감동하다", "en": "to be moved, touched"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "Connective ending listing sequential actions. 보다 → 보고, showing viewing happened before emotional response.", "example_in_sentence": "보고 감동했어요"}]}, {"text": "나이가 많고 아파도 다른 사람을 위해 봉사하는 모습이 훌륭하다고 생각해요.", "translation": "I think it is admirable that he volunteers for others despite being old and in pain.", "vocab": [{"ko": "훌륭하다", "en": "to be admirable; excellent"}, {"ko": "봉사하다", "en": "to volunteer"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어도", "exp": "Concessive ending meaning ''even if'' or ''despite.'' 아프다 → 아파도, showing contrast between difficult circumstances and continued action.", "example_in_sentence": "아파도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present modifier)", "exp": "Verb form used before a noun. 봉사하다 → 봉사하는 모습 (the sight of him volunteering).", "example_in_sentence": "봉사하는 모습"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다고 생각하다", "exp": "Means ''to think that…''. 훌륭하다 → 훌륭하다고 생각해요 (I think it is admirable).", "example_in_sentence": "훌륭하다고 생각해요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "전", "en": "former", "note": ""}, {"ko": "뇌암", "en": "brain cancer", "note": ""}, {"ko": "걸리다", "en": "to contract (disease)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "엉덩이뼈", "en": "hip bone", "note": ""}, {"ko": "다치다", "en": "to be injured", "note": ""}, {"ko": "같다", "en": "to be the same", "note": ""}, {"ko": "넘어지다", "en": "to fall", "note": ""}, {"ko": "꿰매다", "en": "to stitch", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하지만", "en": "but, however", "note": ""}, {"ko": "바로", "en": "immediately, right", "note": ""}, {"ko": "참여하다", "en": "to participate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "집", "en": "house", "note": ""}, {"ko": "짓다", "en": "to build", "note": ""}, {"ko": "부상", "en": "injury", "note": ""}, {"ko": "돕다", "en": "to help", "note": ""}, {"ko": "행동", "en": "action, behavior", "note": ""}, {"ko": "감동하다", "en": "to be moved, touched", "note": ""}, {"ko": "훌륭하다", "en": "to be admirable; excellent", "note": ""}, {"ko": "봉사하다", "en": "to volunteer", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전(前)", "en": "former", "note": "prefix used with titles; 전 대통령 = former president"}, {"ko": "같은 해", "en": "the same year", "note": "해 = year; 같은 = same"}, {"ko": "바늘", "en": "stitch, needle", "note": "바늘을 꿰매다 = to get stitches"}, {"ko": "단체", "en": "organization, group", "note": "비영리 단체 = nonprofit organization"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~어서", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Connective ending indicating sequential or causal relationship. 넘어지다 → 넘어져서, showing that falling caused the need for stitches.", "ex_ko": "같은 해 95세의 나이에 집에서 넘어져서 14바늘을 꿰매야 했어요.", "ex_en": "That same year, at the age of 95, he fell at home and had to get 14 stitches."}, {"name": "~아/어야 하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Auxiliary construction expressing obligation or necessity. 꿰매다 → 꿰매야 하다, meaning ''had to stitch.''", "ex_ko": "같은 해 95세의 나이에 집에서 넘어져서 14바늘을 꿰매야 했어요.", "ex_en": "That same year, at the age of 95, he fell at home and had to get 14 stitches."}, {"name": "~는 (present modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Verb form used before a noun. 봉사하다 → 봉사하는 모습 (the sight of him volunteering).", "ex_ko": "해비타트는 집이 없는 사람들을 위해 집을 짓는 단체예요.", "ex_en": "Habitat is an organization that builds houses for people who do not have homes."}, {"name": "~고", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Connective ending listing sequential actions. 보다 → 보고, showing viewing happened before emotional response.", "ex_ko": "많은 사람들이 그의 행동을 보고 감동했어요.", "ex_en": "Many people saw his actions and were moved."}, {"name": "~아/어도", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Concessive ending meaning ''even if'' or ''despite.'' 아프다 → 아파도, showing contrast between difficult circumstances and continued action.", "ex_ko": "나이가 많고 아파도 다른 사람을 위해 봉사하는 모습이 훌륭하다고 생각해요.", "ex_en": "I think it is admirable that he volunteers for others despite being old and in pain."}, {"name": "~다고 생각하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Means ''to think that…''. 훌륭하다 → 훌륭하다고 생각해요 (I think it is admirable).", "ex_ko": "나이가 많고 아파도 다른 사람을 위해 봉사하는 모습이 훌륭하다고 생각해요.", "ex_en": "I think it is admirable that he volunteers for others despite being old and in pain."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moyxvtj53k6h' and md5(translation) = 'ee3dad91ab50e9faa76d56269cb5ed88';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["There is a very large Guanyin statue on Hainan Island in China, called Nanshan Guanyin.", "The statue is 108 meters tall, which is as high as a 30-story building.", "The Guanyin statue faces the sea and is special because it has three faces.", "Many tourists come to see this statue, which was completed in 2005 and has become a famous tourist destination in China."], "sentences": [{"text": "중국 하이난섬에는 매우 큰 관음상이 있어요.", "translation": "There is a very large Guanyin statue on Hainan Island in China.", "vocab": [{"ko": "중국", "en": "China", "note": "country name"}, {"ko": "매우", "en": "very", "note": "adverb for emphasis"}, {"ko": "크다", "en": "to be big/large", "note": "adjective"}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist/be located", "note": "existence verb"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에는", "exp": "topic particle indicating location", "example_in_sentence": "하이난섬에는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 있다", "exp": "Means ''there is''. 관음상 + 이 있어요 = there is a statue.", "example_in_sentence": "관음상이 있어요"}]}, {"text": "이 관음상의 이름은 난산 관음이에요.", "translation": "This Guanyin statue''s name is Nanshan Guanyin.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이름", "en": "name", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "난산", "en": "Nanshan", "note": "place name"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "possessive particle", "example_in_sentence": "관음상의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~은", "exp": "topic particle", "example_in_sentence": "이름은"}]}, {"text": "관음상의 높이는 108미터예요.", "translation": "The statue''s height is 108 meters.", "vocab": [{"ko": "높이", "en": "height", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "미터", "en": "meter", "note": "unit of measurement"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "possessive particle", "example_in_sentence": "관음상의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~은", "exp": "topic particle", "example_in_sentence": "높이는"}]}, {"text": "이것은 30층 건물만큼 높아요.", "translation": "This is as high as a 30-story building.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이것", "en": "this", "note": "demonstrative pronoun"}, {"ko": "층", "en": "floor/story", "note": "counter for building floors"}, {"ko": "건물", "en": "building", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "높다", "en": "to be high/tall", "note": "adjective"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~만큼", "exp": "Means ''as … as''. 30층 건물만큼 높아요 = as tall as a 30-story building.", "example_in_sentence": "건물만큼"}]}, {"text": "관음상은 바다를 향해 서 있어요.", "translation": "The Guanyin statue faces the sea.", "vocab": [{"ko": "바다", "en": "sea/ocean", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "향하다", "en": "to face/head toward", "note": "verb"}, {"ko": "서다", "en": "to stand", "note": "verb"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 향해", "exp": "Means ''toward'' or ''facing''. 바다를 향해 = facing the sea.", "example_in_sentence": "바다를 향해"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 있다", "exp": "Shows a state that continues after an action. 서다 → 서 있어요 (is standing).", "example_in_sentence": "서 있어요"}]}, {"text": "세 개의 얼굴을 가지고 있어서 특별해요.", "translation": "It is special because it has three faces.", "vocab": [{"ko": "세", "en": "three", "note": "number"}, {"ko": "개", "en": "counter for objects", "note": "general counter"}, {"ko": "얼굴", "en": "face", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "가지다", "en": "to have/possess", "note": "verb"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어서", "exp": "Gives a reason: ''because''. 가지고 있다 → 가지고 있어서 (because it has).", "example_in_sentence": "가지고 있어서"}]}, {"text": "많은 관광객들이 이 관음상을 보러 와요.", "translation": "Many tourists come to see this statue.", "vocab": [{"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many/much", "note": "adjective"}, {"ko": "관광객", "en": "tourist", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to see/look", "note": "verb"}, {"ko": "오다", "en": "to come", "note": "verb"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이", "exp": "subject particle", "example_in_sentence": "관광객들이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을", "exp": "object particle", "example_in_sentence": "관음상을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)러 오다", "exp": "Means ''come (in order) to do''. 보다 → 보러 와요 (come to see).", "example_in_sentence": "보러 와요"}]}, {"text": "2005년에 완성되었고 중국의 유명한 관광지가 되었어요.", "translation": "It was completed in 2005 and has become a famous tourist destination in China.", "vocab": [{"ko": "년", "en": "year", "note": "time unit"}, {"ko": "완성되다", "en": "to be completed", "note": "passive verb"}, {"ko": "유명하다", "en": "to be famous", "note": "adjective"}, {"ko": "관광지", "en": "tourist destination", "note": "noun"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에", "exp": "time particle", "example_in_sentence": "2005년에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "connective ending for sequential actions", "example_in_sentence": "완성되었고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 되다", "exp": "Means ''to become''. 관광지 + 가 되었어요 = became a tourist spot.", "example_in_sentence": "관광지가 되었어요"}]}], "version": "s1"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "중국", "en": "China", "note": "country name"}, {"ko": "매우", "en": "very", "note": "adverb for emphasis"}, {"ko": "크다", "en": "to be big/large", "note": "adjective"}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist/be located", "note": "existence verb"}, {"ko": "이름", "en": "name", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "난산", "en": "Nanshan", "note": "place name"}, {"ko": "높이", "en": "height", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "미터", "en": "meter", "note": "unit of measurement"}, {"ko": "이것", "en": "this", "note": "demonstrative pronoun"}, {"ko": "층", "en": "floor/story", "note": "counter for building floors"}, {"ko": "건물", "en": "building", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "높다", "en": "to be high/tall", "note": "adjective"}, {"ko": "바다", "en": "sea/ocean", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "향하다", "en": "to face/head toward", "note": "verb"}, {"ko": "서다", "en": "to stand", "note": "verb"}, {"ko": "세", "en": "three", "note": "number"}, {"ko": "개", "en": "counter for objects", "note": "general counter"}, {"ko": "얼굴", "en": "face", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "가지다", "en": "to have/possess", "note": "verb"}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many/much", "note": "adjective"}, {"ko": "관광객", "en": "tourist", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to see/look", "note": "verb"}, {"ko": "오다", "en": "to come", "note": "verb"}, {"ko": "년", "en": "year", "note": "time unit"}, {"ko": "완성되다", "en": "to be completed", "note": "passive verb"}, {"ko": "유명하다", "en": "to be famous", "note": "adjective"}, {"ko": "관광지", "en": "tourist destination", "note": "noun"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~에는", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "topic particle indicating location", "ex_ko": "중국 하이난섬에는 매우 큰 관음상이 있어요.", "ex_en": "There is a very large Guanyin statue on Hainan Island in China."}, {"name": "~이/가 있다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''there is''. 관음상 + 이 있어요 = there is a statue.", "ex_ko": "중국 하이난섬에는 매우 큰 관음상이 있어요.", "ex_en": "There is a very large Guanyin statue on Hainan Island in China."}, {"name": "~의", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "possessive particle", "ex_ko": "이 관음상의 이름은 난산 관음이에요.", "ex_en": "This Guanyin statue''s name is Nanshan Guanyin."}, {"name": "~은", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "topic particle", "ex_ko": "이 관음상의 이름은 난산 관음이에요.", "ex_en": "This Guanyin statue''s name is Nanshan Guanyin."}, {"name": "~만큼", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''as … as''. 30층 건물만큼 높아요 = as tall as a 30-story building.", "ex_ko": "이것은 30층 건물만큼 높아요.", "ex_en": "This is as high as a 30-story building."}, {"name": "~을/를 향해", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''toward'' or ''facing''. 바다를 향해 = facing the sea.", "ex_ko": "관음상은 바다를 향해 서 있어요.", "ex_en": "The Guanyin statue faces the sea."}, {"name": "~아/어 있다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Shows a state that continues after an action. 서다 → 서 있어요 (is standing).", "ex_ko": "관음상은 바다를 향해 서 있어요.", "ex_en": "The Guanyin statue faces the sea."}, {"name": "~아/어서", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Gives a reason: ''because''. 가지고 있다 → 가지고 있어서 (because it has).", "ex_ko": "세 개의 얼굴을 가지고 있어서 특별해요.", "ex_en": "It is special because it has three faces."}, {"name": "~이", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "subject particle", "ex_ko": "많은 관광객