oing / start to do''. 쉬다 → 쉬기 시작하다 = ''start breathing / began to breathe''.", "ex_ko": "2분 후에 개가 다시 숨을 쉬기 시작했어요.", "ex_en": "After 2 minutes, the dog began breathing again."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mozbw80uixss' and md5(translation) = 'cb3515e79694c1edb429b8bdbb326f7b';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"sentences": [{"text": "분재는 작은 화분에서 키우는 나무예요.", "idx": 0, "translation": "Bonsai is a tree grown in a small pot.", "vocab": [{"ko": "분재", "en": "bonsai", "note": "ornamental miniature tree art form"}, {"ko": "화분", "en": "pot; flower pot", "note": "container for plants"}, {"ko": "키우다", "en": "to grow; to raise; to cultivate", "note": "transitive verb for nurturing plants/animals"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present modifier)", "exp": "Verb form used before a noun. 키우다 → 키우는 나무 (a tree that people grow).", "example_in_sentence": "키우는 나무"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (location / place where action occurs)", "exp": "in / at (locative particle for the site of action)", "example_in_sentence": "화분에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~예요 (polite copula / present tense of 이다)", "exp": "is (statement in casual-polite register)", "example_in_sentence": "나무예요"}]}, {"text": "이 분재 나무는 400년이 넘었어요.", "idx": 1, "translation": "This bonsai tree is over 400 years old.", "vocab": [{"ko": "넘다", "en": "to exceed; to go over; to pass", "note": "verb meaning surpass a threshold"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 넘다", "exp": "Means ''to be over'' an amount. 400년이 넘었어요 = it is over 400 years old.", "example_in_sentence": "400년이 넘었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense, casual-polite)", "exp": "did / has been (perfect aspect)", "example_in_sentence": "넘었어요"}]}, {"text": "일본에서 온 이 나무는 아주 특별해요.", "idx": 2, "translation": "This tree that came from Japan is very special.", "vocab": [{"ko": "오다", "en": "to come; to arrive", "note": "directional verb"}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": "adjective meaning distinct or noteworthy"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past modifier)", "exp": "Past form of a verb used before a noun. 오다 → 온 (that came). 일본에서 온 나무 = a tree that came from Japan.", "example_in_sentence": "온 이 나무"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (from; origin particle)", "exp": "from (origin/source in this context)", "example_in_sentence": "일본에서"}]}, {"text": "많은 사람들이 이 나무를 보러 와요.", "idx": 3, "translation": "Many people come to see this tree.", "vocab": [{"ko": "많다", "en": "many; much; a lot", "note": "adjective / modifier"}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to see; to watch; to look at", "note": "perception verb"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)러 오다", "exp": "Means ''come to do''. 보다 → 보러 와요 (come to see).", "example_in_sentence": "보러 와요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (direct object particle)", "exp": "marks the object of the action (see)", "example_in_sentence": "이 나무를"}]}, {"text": "분재를 키우는 것은 쉽지 않아요.", "idx": 4, "translation": "Growing bonsai is not easy.", "vocab": [{"ko": "키우다", "en": "to grow; to raise; to cultivate", "note": "transitive verb"}, {"ko": "쉽다", "en": "to be easy", "note": "adjective"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것", "exp": "Turns a verb into a noun: ''doing''. 키우다 → 키우는 것 (growing). 은 marks it as the topic.", "example_in_sentence": "키우는 것은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않다 (negation)", "exp": "is not; negative form of adjective/verb", "example_in_sentence": "쉽지 않아요"}]}, {"text": "물을 주고 가지를 잘라야 해요.", "idx": 5, "translation": "You must give it water and cut the branches.", "vocab": [{"ko": "물", "en": "water", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "주다", "en": "to give; to supply", "note": "transitive verb"}, {"ko": "가지", "en": "branch", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "자르다", "en": "to cut", "note": "transitive verb"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 (coordinate; ''and'' / addition)", "exp": "and (conjoins two sequential or parallel actions)", "example_in_sentence": "물을 주고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어야 하다", "exp": "Means ''must'' or ''have to''. 자르다 → 잘라야 해요 (must cut; 르 becomes ㄹㄹ).", "example_in_sentence": "잘라야 해요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "Object particle: marks what the action is done to. 물을 주다 = give water; 가지를 자르다 = cut branches.", "example_in_sentence": "가지를"}]}, {"text": "매일 정성껏 돌봐야 해요.", "idx": 6, "translation": "You have to take good care of it every day.", "vocab": [{"ko": "매일", "en": "every day; daily", "note": "adverb of frequency"}, {"ko": "정성껏", "en": "sincerely; with devotion; earnestly", "note": "adverb expressing wholehearted effort"}, {"ko": "돌보다", "en": "to care for; to look after; to tend", "note": "verb meaning nurture/attend to"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어야 하다 (obligation; must)", "exp": "must; have to", "example_in_sentence": "돌봐야 해요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "정성껏 돌보다", "exp": "care for with sincerity / devotion (fixed collocation)", "example_in_sentence": "정성껏 돌봐야"}]}, {"text": "이런 오래된 분재는 정말 귀해요.", "idx": 7, "translation": "Such old bonsai are truly rare.", "vocab": [{"ko": "오래되다", "en": "to be old; to age", "note": "adjective/verb meaning aged or ancient"}, {"ko": "귀하다", "en": "to be rare; precious", "note": "adjective meaning scarce or precious"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past modifier)", "exp": "Past form of a verb used before a noun. 오래되다 → 오래된 분재 (an old bonsai).", "example_in_sentence": "오래된 분재"}]}, {"text": "400년 동안 살아있다는 것이 놀라워요.", "idx": 8, "translation": "The fact that it has been alive for 400 years is amazing.", "vocab": [{"ko": "살아있다", "en": "to be alive; to live", "note": "verb meaning exist as living being"}, {"ko": "동안", "en": "during; for (time period); while", "note": "noun/postposition marking duration"}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be amazing; surprising", "note": "verb expressing wonder or astonishment"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~다는 것 (that-clause; nominalization of statement)", "exp": "the fact/thing that (quoted statement nominalized)", "example_in_sentence": "살아있다는 것"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~동안 (during; for the duration of)", "exp": "during / over a span of time", "example_in_sentence": "400년 동안"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "ㅂ irregular", "exp": "놀랍다 is ㅂ-irregular: ㅂ becomes 우 before 어요. 놀랍다 → 놀라워요 (it''s amazing).", "example_in_sentence": "놀라워요"}]}], "version": "s1"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "분재", "en": "bonsai", "note": "ornamental miniature tree art form"}, {"ko": "화분", "en": "pot; flower pot", "note": "container for plants"}, {"ko": "키우다", "en": "to grow; to raise; to cultivate", "note": "transitive verb for nurturing plants/animals"}, {"ko": "넘다", "en": "to exceed; to go over; to pass", "note": "verb meaning surpass a threshold"}, {"ko": "오다", "en": "to come; to arrive", "note": "directional verb"}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": "adjective meaning distinct or noteworthy"}, {"ko": "많다", "en": "many; much; a lot", "note": "adjective / modifier"}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to see; to watch; to look at", "note": "perception verb"}, {"ko": "쉽다", "en": "to be easy", "note": "adjective"}, {"ko": "물", "en": "water", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "주다", "en": "to give; to supply", "note": "transitive verb"}, {"ko": "가지", "en": "branch", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "자르다", "en": "to cut", "note": "transitive verb"}, {"ko": "매일", "en": "every day; daily", "note": "adverb of frequency"}, {"ko": "정성껏", "en": "sincerely; with devotion; earnestly", "note": "adverb expressing wholehearted effort"}, {"ko": "돌보다", "en": "to care for; to look after; to tend", "note": "verb meaning nurture/attend to"}, {"ko": "오래되다", "en": "to be old; to age", "note": "adjective/verb meaning aged or ancient"}, {"ko": "귀하다", "en": "to be rare; precious", "note": "adjective meaning scarce or precious"}, {"ko": "살아있다", "en": "to be alive; to live", "note": "verb meaning exist as living being"}, {"ko": "동안", "en": "during; for (time period); while", "note": "noun/postposition marking duration"}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be amazing; surprising", "note": "verb expressing wonder or astonishment"}, {"ko": "나무", "en": "tree", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일본", "en": "Japan", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이런", "en": "such, this kind of", "note": ""}, {"ko": "살다", "en": "to live", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~는 (present modifier)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Verb form used before a noun. 키우다 → 키우는 나무 (a tree that people grow).", "ex_ko": "분재는 작은 화분에서 키우는 나무예요.", "ex_en": "Bonsai is a tree grown in a small pot."}, {"name": "~에서 (location / place where action occurs)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "in / at (locative particle for the site of action)", "ex_ko": "분재는 작은 화분에서 키우는 나무예요.", "ex_en": "Bonsai is a tree grown in a small pot."}, {"name": "~예요 (polite copula / present tense of 이다)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "is (statement in casual-polite register)", "ex_ko": "분재는 작은 화분에서 키우는 나무예요.", "ex_en": "Bonsai is a tree grown in a small pot."}, {"name": "~이/가 넘다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Means ''to be over'' an amount. 400년이 넘었어요 = it is over 400 years old.", "ex_ko": "이 분재 나무는 400년이 넘었어요.", "ex_en": "This bonsai tree is over 400 years old."}, {"name": "~았/었어요 (past tense, casual-polite)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "did / has been (perfect aspect)", "ex_ko": "이 분재 나무는 400년이 넘었어요.", "ex_en": "This bonsai tree is over 400 years old."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past modifier)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Past form of a verb used before a noun. 오다 → 온 (that came). 일본에서 온 나무 = a tree that came from Japan.", "ex_ko": "일본에서 온 이 나무는 아주 특별해요.", "ex_en": "This tree that came from Japan is very special."}, {"name": "~(으)러 오다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Means ''come to do''. 보다 → 보러 와요 (come to see).", "ex_ko": "많은 사람들이 이 나무를 보러 와요.", "ex_en": "Many people come to see this tree."}, {"name": "~을/를 (direct object particle)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Object particle: marks what the action is done to. 물을 주다 = give water; 가지를 자르다 = cut branches.", "ex_ko": "많은 사람들이 이 나무를 보러 와요.", "ex_en": "Many people come to see this tree."}, {"name": "~는 것", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Turns a verb into a noun: ''doing''. 키우다 → 키우는 것 (growing). 은 marks it as the topic.", "ex_ko": "분재를 키우는 것은 쉽지 않아요.", "ex_en": "Growing bonsai is not easy."}, {"name": "~지 않다 (negation)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "is not; negative form of adjective/verb", "ex_ko": "분재를 키우는 것은 쉽지 않아요.", "ex_en": "Growing bonsai is not easy."}, {"name": "~고 (coordinate; ''and'' / addition)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "and (conjoins two sequential or parallel actions)", "ex_ko": "물을 주고 가지를 잘라야 해요.", "ex_en": "You must give it water and cut the branches."}, {"name": "~아/어야 하다 (obligation; must)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Means ''must'' or ''have to''. 자르다 → 잘라야 해요 (must cut; 르 becomes ㄹㄹ).", "ex_ko": "물을 주고 가지를 잘라야 해요.", "ex_en": "You must give it water and cut the branches."}, {"name": "~다는 것 (that-clause; nominalization of statement)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "the fact/thing that (quoted statement nominalized)", "ex_ko": "400년 동안 살아있다는 것이 놀라워요.", "ex_en": "The fact that it has been alive for 400 years is amazing."}, {"name": "~동안 (during; for the duration of)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "during / over a span of time", "ex_ko": "400년 동안 살아있다는 것이 놀라워요.", "ex_en": "The fact that it has been alive for 400 years is amazing."}, {"name": "ㅂ irregular", "level": "Starter", "exp": "놀랍다 is ㅂ-irregular: ㅂ becomes 우 before 어요. 놀랍다 → 놀라워요 (it''s amazing).", "ex_ko": "400년 동안 살아있다는 것이 놀라워요.", "ex_en": "The fact that it has been alive for 400 years is amazing."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mozbwz4gw5d4' and md5(translation) = '568a0aedf2fc14b288cca181febf0b4c';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"sentences": [{"text": "유럽에는 오래된 다리 위에 새로운 다리를 지은 곳이 있어요.", "idx": 0, "translation": "In Europe, there is a place where a new bridge was built on top of an old bridge.", "vocab": [{"ko": "유럽", "en": "Europe", "note": "proper noun"}, {"ko": "오래되다", "en": "to be old", "note": "adjective; 오래된 = old (modifier form)"}, {"ko": "다리", "en": "bridge", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past modifier)", "exp": "Past form of a verb used before a noun. 오래되다 → 오래된 다리 (an old bridge).", "example_in_sentence": "오래된 다리"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "ㅂ irregular + ~(으)ㄴ", "exp": "새롭다 → 새로운 다리 (a new bridge): ㅂ becomes 우 before the modifier.", "example_in_sentence": "새로운 다리"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "ㅅ irregular + ~(으)ㄴ", "exp": "짓다 (to build) is ㅅ-irregular: ㅅ drops before 은. 짓다 → 지은 곳 (a place where … was built).", "example_in_sentence": "지은 곳"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 있다", "exp": "Means ''there is''. 곳 + 이 있어요 = there is a place.", "example_in_sentence": "곳이 있어요"}]}, {"text": "12세기에 만든 돌 다리가 가장 아래에 있어요.", "idx": 1, "translation": "The stone bridge made in the 12th century is at the very bottom.", "vocab": [{"ko": "세기", "en": "century", "note": ""}, {"ko": "돌", "en": "stone", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가장", "en": "the most; the very", "note": "adverb of degree"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past modifier)", "exp": "Past form of a verb used before a noun. 만들다 → 만든 (made); the ㄹ drops before ㄴ.", "example_in_sentence": "만든 돌 다리"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 있다", "exp": "to be at/in (location)", "example_in_sentence": "가장 아래에 있어요"}]}, {"text": "18세기에 사람들이 더 큰 다리가 필요했어요.", "idx": 2, "translation": "In the 18th century, people needed a bigger bridge.", "vocab": [{"ko": "필요하다", "en": "to need", "note": ""}, {"ko": "크다", "en": "to be big", "note": "크다 → 더 큰 (comparative)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Adjective form used before a noun. 크다 → 큰 (big). 더 큰 다리 = a bigger bridge.", "example_in_sentence": "더 큰 다리"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "past tense", "example_in_sentence": "필요했어요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "더 + adjective", "exp": "comparative form", "example_in_sentence": "더 큰"}]}, {"text": "그래서 옛날 다리를 부수지 않고 그 위에 새 다리를 만들었어요.", "idx": 3, "translation": "So they didn''t demolish the old bridge but built a new bridge on top of it.", "vocab": [{"ko": "옛날", "en": "old times; formerly", "note": "noun"}, {"ko": "부수다", "en": "to demolish; to break", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않고", "exp": "negation + coordination (not doing but doing something else)", "example_in_sentence": "부수지 않고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "N 위에", "exp": "위 means ''top''. 그 위에 = on top of it.", "example_in_sentence": "그 위에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "past tense", "example_in_sentence": "만들었어요"}]}, {"text": "20세기에도 똑같은 일이 일어났어요.", "idx": 4, "translation": "In the 20th century, the same thing happened.", "vocab": [{"ko": "똑같다", "en": "to be the same; identical", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에도", "exp": "also; even (particle 도 on ~에)", "example_in_sentence": "20세기에도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "Adjective form used before a noun. 똑같다 → 똑같은 일 (the same thing).", "example_in_sentence": "똑같은 일"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "past tense", "example_in_sentence": "일어났어요"}]}, {"text": "차가 많아져서 더 넓은 다리가 필요했거든요.", "idx": 5, "translation": "Cars increased, so a wider bridge was needed.", "vocab": [{"ko": "차", "en": "car; vehicle", "note": ""}, {"ko": "많아지다", "en": "to increase; become many", "note": "~져서 = contraction of ~게 되어서"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어서", "exp": "Gives a reason: ''so'' or ''because''. 많아지다 → 많아져서 (because there were more cars).", "example_in_sentence": "많아져서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~거든요", "exp": "because; since (informal causal ending)", "example_in_sentence": "필요했거든요"}]}, {"text": "그래서 또 다시 위에 새 다리를 지었어요.", "idx": 6, "translation": "So they built a new bridge on top again.", "vocab": [{"ko": "또 다시", "en": "again; once more", "note": "emphatic repetition"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense. 짓다 is ㅅ-irregular: ㅅ drops before a vowel, so 짓다 → 지었어요 (built).", "example_in_sentence": "지었어요"}]}, {"text": "지금은 세 개의 다리가 층층이 쌓여 있어요.", "idx": 7, "translation": "Now three bridges are stacked layer upon layer.", "vocab": [{"ko": "세 개", "en": "three (items)", "note": "counter form"}, {"ko": "층층이", "en": "layer upon layer; in layers", "note": "adverb"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 있다", "exp": "Shows a state that continues after an action. 쌓이다 → 쌓여 있어요 (are stacked).", "example_in_sentence": "쌓여 있어요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "층층이 쌓이다", "exp": "to stack layer by layer", "example_in_sentence": "층층이 쌓여 있어요"}]}, {"text": "가장 오래된 다리는 800년이 넘었어요.", "idx": 8, "translation": "The oldest bridge is over 800 years old.", "vocab": [{"ko": "넘다", "en": "to exceed; to go over", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past modifier)", "exp": "Past form of a verb used before a noun. 오래되다 → 오래된 (old). 가장 오래된 다리 = the oldest bridge.", "example_in_sentence": "가장 오래된 다리"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "past tense", "example_in_sentence": "넘었어요"}]}, {"text": "옛날 것을 보호하면서 새로운 것을 만든 좋은 예시예요.", "idx": 9, "translation": "It is a good example of protecting the old while making the new.", "vocab": [{"ko": "보호하다", "en": "to protect", "note": ""}, {"ko": "예시", "en": "example", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면서", "exp": "Means ''while'': doing two things at once. 보호하다 → 보호하면서 (while protecting).", "example_in_sentence": "보호하면서"}]}], "version": "s1"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "유럽", "en": "Europe", "note": "proper noun"}, {"ko": "오래되다", "en": "to be old", "note": "adjective; 오래된 = old 