en (particle 도 on ~에)", "ex_ko": "20세기에도 똑같은 일이 일어났어요.", "ex_en": "In the 20th century, the same thing happened."}, {"name": "~아/어서", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Gives a reason: ''so'' or ''because''. 많아지다 → 많아져서 (because there were more cars).", "ex_ko": "차가 많아져서 더 넓은 다리가 필요했거든요.", "ex_en": "Cars increased, so a wider bridge was needed."}, {"name": "~거든요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "because; since (informal causal ending)", "ex_ko": "차가 많아져서 더 넓은 다리가 필요했거든요.", "ex_en": "Cars increased, so a wider bridge was needed."}, {"name": "~아/어 있다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Shows a state that continues after an action. 쌓이다 → 쌓여 있어요 (are stacked).", "ex_ko": "지금은 세 개의 다리가 층층이 쌓여 있어요.", "ex_en": "Now three bridges are stacked layer upon layer."}, {"name": "~(으)면서", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''while'': doing two things at once. 보호하다 → 보호하면서 (while protecting).", "ex_ko": "옛날 것을 보호하면서 새로운 것을 만든 좋은 예시예요.", "ex_en": "It is a good example of protecting the old while making the new."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mozbxv0rect2' and md5(translation) = '639300d91f96b8a4780b7d58b5a1ceac';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"sentences": [{"text": "한 남자가 아들과 함께 찍은 사진을 공개했어요.", "idx": 0, "translation": "A man publicly shared a photo taken with his son.", "vocab": [{"ko": "공개하다", "en": "to make public, to reveal", "note": "past tense: 공개했어요"}, {"ko": "사진", "en": "photograph, picture", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아들", "en": "son", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past modifier)", "exp": "Past form of a verb used before a noun. 찍다 → 찍은 사진 (a photo that was taken).", "example_in_sentence": "찍은 사진"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense polite ending)", "exp": "Completed action in polite conversational style.", "example_in_sentence": "공개했어요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~과/와 함께", "exp": "Together with, along with.", "example_in_sentence": "아들과 함께"}]}, {"text": "29년 전에 찍은 사진과 똑같은 포즈로 다시 찍었어요.", "idx": 1, "translation": "He took a photo again in exactly the same pose as the one taken 29 years ago.", "vocab": [{"ko": "포즈", "en": "pose, posture", "note": "borrowed English word"}, {"ko": "찍다", "en": "to take (a photo), to shoot", "note": ""}, {"ko": "똑같다", "en": "to be identical, exactly the same", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past modifier)", "exp": "Past form of a verb used before a noun. 29년 전에 찍은 사진 = the photo taken 29 years ago.", "example_in_sentence": "29년 전에 찍은 사진"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense polite ending)", "exp": "Completed action in polite conversational style.", "example_in_sentence": "찍었어요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~(으)로", "exp": "Shows the way something is done. 똑같은 포즈로 = in the same pose.", "example_in_sentence": "똑같은 포즈로"}]}, {"text": "첫 번째 사진에서 아버지는 젊고 아들은 아기였어요.", "idx": 2, "translation": "In the first photo, the father was young and the son was a baby.", "vocab": [{"ko": "첫 번째", "en": "first, the first", "note": "ordinal number"}, {"ko": "아버지", "en": "father", "note": ""}, {"ko": "젊다", "en": "to be young", "note": ""}], "